Stephanus Zubrinic||son of ahnentafel 10 and 11, brother of ahnentafel 5|baptism|3 July 1856|Otocac|Otocac baptisms entry 49 - "Rustici Confiniarii e Sumecica N. 2 ... Nicolaus Zubrinic et ejus uxor Anna nata Strumbulko"; ark 3:1:3QSQ-G99C-PK2C

# Otočac, the Michael Žubrinić households of 1846-58 (read 15 September 2026).
# Fourteen of fifteen indexed entries were read; nine of those children are already
# in the tree. These five are not. Every one of them has siblings who ARE in the
# tree, so these are gaps in known families rather than an unknown branch.
Maria Magdalena Theresia Žubrinić||daughter of Michaël Žubrinić and Maria Marković, Otočac|baptism|21 July 1846|Otočac|Rodjeni 1846-1858 - Conditio «Agricola Confiniarius», no village or house number given; ark 3:1:3QS7-899C-G5D9
Mathias Žubrinić||son of Michael Žubrinić and Maria Marković, Šumećica N° 5|baptism|3 January 1855|Šumećica, Otočac|Rodjeni 1846-1858 - «Confiniarius e Sumećica N° 5», first entry of 1855 below the year rule; ark 3:1:3QS7-899C-PVT8
Josephus Žubrinić||son of Michael Žubrinić and Maria Rogić, Prozor N° 50|baptism|3 July 1855|Prozor, Otočac|Rodjeni 1846-1858 - «Miles Gregarius e Prozor N° 50»; brother of Nikola Miko b. 8 Jan 1858, who is in the tree; ark 3:1:3QSQ-G99C-PK64
Stephanus Žubrinić||son of Michael Žubrinić and Maria Marković, Šumećica N° 5|baptism|17 December 1858|Šumećica, Otočac|Rodjeni 1846-1858 p. 290 - «Rusticus e Sumećica N° 5»; brother of Marta 1849 and Magdalena 1852, who are in the tree; ark 3:1:3QS7-899C-PVGY
Maria Žubrinić||daughter of Michael Žubrinić and Magdalena Glavinić, Prozor N° 49|baptism|28 November 1858|Prozor, Otočac|Rodjeni 1846-1858 - «Rustica e Prozor N° 49»; surname written Žubrinić on the page where the index reads «Dubrinić»; ark 3:1:3QS7-899C-PVLN
Mare Antić||daughter of Josip (ahnentafel 24) and Maria Antić, Selce N° 74; sister of ahnentafel 12|death|21 October 1850|Selce|LIBER DEFUNCTORUM p. 99 - «Preminu Osip Antić težak i Mare kćer», aged 6, «Od kolere», father and daughter in one entry; ark 3:1:3QSQ-G99X-13PY
Matilda Papić||third name on the stone cross of Josip Papić (ahnentafel 6) and Antonija — almost certainly their daughter|memorial|died 1921, born 1895|Senj|Senj municipal cemetery, «MATILDA ✽1895 †1921», read at 4x. NOT IN THE TREE UNDER THIS NAME: the tree has two Papić daughters born 1895 — Franka (20 Jan) and Sulka (7 Feb) — and neither has a death recorded. One of them may be this woman; IMG_8131
Antonius Gergacs||son of Nicolaus Gerkacs (ahnentafel 220), and therefore a brother of ahnentafel 110|named in his father's death entry|30 October 1783|Karlobag|Karlobag Umrli 1774-1804 folio 39 — his father «obiit … in domo filij sui Antonij», died in this son's house. Not in the published tree; the Gerkacs collaterals are not published at all; ark 3:1:3QS7-L99C-GSBH
Margaritha Smojver||daughter of ahnentafel 212 and 213|baptism|9 July 1764|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed, entry 270 — «Entry for Margaritham Smoiver and Josephi Smoiver»; mother Antoniae. ark 1:1:QKMX-YLY7. Born twelve years after her parents' marriage of 20 Nov 1752 and twelve years before her father's death in 1776
Joseip Pekasu||son of Šimun Pekas of Karlobag; candidate brother of ahnentafel 213|baptism|1 March 1705|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Parents Šimun Pekasu». The earliest Pekas entry found; his own daughter Antonia is baptised 1742
Margarita Pekasa||daughter of Šimun Pekas of Karlobag; candidate sister of ahnentafel 213|baptism|28 October 1719|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Parents Simon Pekasa», no mother named
Katarina Pekasa||daughter of Šimun Pekas and STOJA; candidate half-sister of ahnentafel 213|baptism|19 June 1734|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Parents Stoja, Simuna Pekasa». The mother is NOT Mare
Perina Pekasa||daughter of Šimun Pekas and MARE; candidate sister of ahnentafel 213|baptism|29 June 1738|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Parents Simuna Pekasa, Mare». Mare is the only wife named that matches ahnentafel 427, Mara Pekass
Antonia Pehasa||daughter of Osip Pekas and Monde, Karlobag — explicitly NOT ahnentafel 213|baptism|18 January 1742|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Parents Monde, Osipa Pehasa». Recorded here to rule her out: ahnentafel 213 married in 1752 and bore a son in 1754, so a girl baptised 1742 cannot be her
Antonü Bechi (Bacchi)||second son of ahnentafel 428 and 429, and not in the tree|baptism|11 September 1780|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Angelo Bechi × Catharina», ark 1:1:QKMX-B9R1. A brother of ahnentafel 214, born twenty months after him under the same two parents
Hevam Uroda||daughter of ahnentafel 108 and 109, and not in the tree|baptism|September 1773|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Georgio Uroda × Maria». THE SECOND OF THAT NAME: Heva Joanna was baptised to the same couple on 28 December 1769, so either the first died and the name was reused, or the index holds one child twice
Mikola Luckinicha||son of a Vicko Luckinić of Karlobag; CANDIDATE elder brother of ahnentafel 105|baptism|9 December 1719|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Parents Vicka Luckinicha», no mother named; ark 1:1:QKMX-YTMT
Magdalenam Gergacs||daughter of ahnentafel 110 and 111, and not in the tree|baptism|11 March 1787|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Michaële Gergacs × Lucia»; ark 1:1:QKMX-BCZC
Magdalenam Gargacs||SECOND daughter of that name to ahnentafel 110 and 111 — a necronym, or the index holding one child twice|baptism|January 1792|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Michaele Gargacs × Lucia»; ark 1:1:QKMX-Y1CM. The first Magdalena was baptised 11 March 1787
Catharinam Gergacz||daughter of ahnentafel 110 and 111, and not in the tree|baptism|25 November 1794|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Michaële Gergacz × Luciæ»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YVGM
Bartholomæum Gergacs||son of ahnentafel 110 and 111, and not in the tree|baptism|17 August 1797|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Michaelo Gergacs × Luciæ»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YBDF
Mathiam Gergacs||son of ahnentafel 110 and 111, and not in the tree|baptism|23 February 1801|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Michaële Gergacs × Lucia»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YK1J
Mariæ Vukich||daughter of ahnentafel 106 and 107, indexed under their BY-NAME|baptism|6 May 1776|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Vincentio Vukich × Oliva»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YF7B. The 1781 reading of their daughter Oliva gives them as «Vincentio, et Oliva Smoyver, VULGÒ VUKIĆ, Conjugibus», so Vukich is this couple's recorded house name
Josephi Francisci Vukich||son of ahnentafel 106 and 107, indexed under their BY-NAME|baptism|August 1777|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Vincentio Vukich × Oliva»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YFJS
Anna Oliva Vukics||daughter of ahnentafel 106 and 107, indexed under their BY-NAME|baptism|25 September 1785|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Vincentio Vukics × Oliva»; ark 1:1:QKMX-B3LJ
Smojuer (no given name in the index)||child of ahnentafel 106 and 107, and not in the tree|baptism|23 February 1782|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Vincentio Smojuer × Oliva»; ark 1:1:QKMX-BCN6. The index carries no given name for this child
Vincentiam Luciam Smoÿver||daughter of ahnentafel 106 and 107, and not in the tree|baptism|5 December 1788|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Vincentio Smoÿver × Oliva»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YJ2M
Michael Sekula||son of ahnentafel 42 and 43, and not in the tree|baptism|26 September 1841|Otočac|Otočac births, indexed — «Marcus Sekula × Lucia»; ark 1:1:QKMK-SKPG. The couple is indexed under BOTH surnames, and the tree itself carries two of their children as «Orešković Oreskovic Sekula»
Paulus Sekula||son of ahnentafel 42 and 43, and not in the tree — TWIN of Petrus|baptism|29 June 1846|Otočac|Otočac births, indexed — «Marcus Sekula × Lucia»; ark 1:1:QKMK-SQML. Petrus, whom the tree has, was baptised the SAME DAY to the same parents: ark 1:1:QKMK-SQMV. Twins, not a duplicate
Mariam Catharinam Pilipich||daughter of ahnentafel 26 and 27, and not in the tree|baptism|25 January 1834|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Vincentü Pilipich × Matthææ Urade»; ark 1:1:QKMX-BJJT. Four years before ahnentafel 13
Georgium Pilipich||son of ahnentafel 26 and 27, and not in the tree|baptism|18 November 1841|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Vincentü Pilipich × Mathiæ Uroda»; ark 1:1:QKMX-BQD8
Georgius Perpić||son of ahnentafel 14 and 15; CANDIDATE younger brother of ahnentafel 7|baptism|22 April 1868|Krivi Put|Krivi Put births, indexed — «Joannes Perpić × Lucia Perpić»; ark 1:1:XQM9-ZVQK. A CANDIDATE: Prpić is the dominant surname of this parish and the index holds several Perpić × Perpić couples. What supports it is that the same couple's Stephanus of 1861 IS in the tree
Joanna Perpić||daughter of ahnentafel 14 and 15; CANDIDATE younger sister of ahnentafel 7|baptism|12 January 1874|Krivi Put|Krivi Put births, indexed — born 6 Jan 1874, «Joannes Perpić × Lucia Perpić»; ark 1:1:XQM9-XB9Q. Same caution as Georgius
Josephus Perpić||son of ahnentafel 14 and 15; CANDIDATE younger brother of ahnentafel 7|baptism|7 July 1876|Krivi Put|Krivi Put births, indexed — «Joannes Perpić × Lucia»; ark 1:1:XQM9-J5PG. Same caution, and the mother is given only as Lucia
Dominicum Bartholomæum Uroda||son of ahnentafel 54 and 55, and not in the tree — brother of ahnentafel 27|baptism|24 August 1812|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Georgio Uroda × Maria»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YGZF. Ahnentafel 54 was baptised «Joannis Georgij» and is named alive in 1834 as «piscatoris GEORGII Uroda», so the index's Georgius is him. Two years after ahnentafel 27, to the same couple
Margaritha Maria Uroda||daughter of ahnentafel 54's BROTHER Joannis, not of ahnentafel 54|baptism|15 February 1810|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Joanne Uroda × Maria»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YG4K. She CANNOT be ahnentafel 55's: ahnentafel 27 was born to her on 23 April 1810, nine weeks later. The father is the brother baptised 1784, who married Maria filia Nicolai Barletich on 10 February 1806
Joannem Bartholomæum Stanislaum Uroda||son of ahnentafel 54's BROTHER Joannis|baptism|25 August 1811|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Joanne Uroda × Maria»; ark 1:1:QKMX-BV6R. Same household as Margaritha of 1810 — the brother's, not ahnentafel 54's
Hevam Vuhich||daughter of ahnentafel 212 and 213, indexed under their BY-NAME; CANDIDATE|baptism|10 April 1766|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Josephi Vuhich × Antoniæ»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YYFL. Ahnentafel 212's death entry of 1776 is «Josephus Smojver dictus VUKCICH», so Vukić is this man's recorded house name
Joannæ Vukich||daughter of ahnentafel 212 and 213, indexed under their BY-NAME; CANDIDATE|baptism|16 May 1770|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Josepho Vukich × Antonia»; ark 1:1:QKMX-BZ42
Simonem Pillopich||brother of ahnentafel 52, son of ahnentafel 104 and 105|baptism|21 October 1758|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Jacobi Pillopich × Catharina»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YDW1
Franciscum Pillepich||brother of ahnentafel 52, son of ahnentafel 104 and 105|baptism|28 July 1762|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Jacobi Pillepich × Catharinæ»; ark 1:1:QKMX-BSB4
Simolicianum Pillepich||brother of ahnentafel 52, son of ahnentafel 104 and 105|baptism|1 March 1765|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Jacobi Pillepich × Catharinæ»; ark 1:1:QKMX-BMMQ
Antonia Pekasovicha||daughter of Šimun Pekas of Karlobag — explicitly NOT ahnentafel 213|baptism|25 October 1711|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Father Simuna Pekasovicha», no mother named; ark 1:1:QKMX-YSF2. Recorded here to rule her out, as the second of two: ahnentafel 213 bore Margaritha in 1764 and Joanna in 1770, which this Antonia would have done at 53 and 59. A sixth spelling of the surname
Margaritam Antich||daughter of a Josephus Antić of Selce — NOT of ahnentafel 24|baptism|7 November 1844|Selce|Selce births, indexed — «Father Josephi Antich, Mother Margaritæ»; ark 1:1:QKMJ-MSB9. Recorded to rule her out: ahnentafel 24's wife is Maria Jelličić, not Margarita, and he died in 1850 with Maria outliving him to 1882, so there was no second marriage. Found by a place-only probe after this parish was recorded as unindexed under the surname Antić
Martha Perpič||daughter of ahnentafel 14 and 15; CANDIDATE elder sister of ahnentafel 7|baptism|29 July 1853|Krivi Put|Krivi Put births, indexed — «Ivana Perpič × Lucia Perpič»; ark 1:1:XQM9-ZV9G. CANDIDATE only: at least two Joannes Perpić households sit at Krivi Put in this decade, one of them married to a Francisca
Tomu Perpić||son of ahnentafel 14 and 15; CANDIDATE elder brother of ahnentafel 7|baptism|14 December 1856|Krivi Put|Krivi Put births, indexed — «Ivana Perpić × Luce Perpić»; ark 1:1:XQM9-C5W2. CANDIDATE only, for the same reason as Martha 1853
Josephus Tomlienevics||son of a Paulus Tomljanović of Karlobag; CANDIDATE brother of ahnentafel 111|baptism|July 1784|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Pauli Tomlienevics × Thomæ»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YJ95. CANDIDATE ONLY: ahnentafel 111's mother is unknown, so nothing ties her to a Thoma, and a SECOND Paulus Tomljanović is fathering at Karlobag in the same years by a Catharina
Joannam Tomljenovich||daughter of a Paulus Tomljanović of Karlobag; CANDIDATE sister of ahnentafel 111|baptism|June 1787|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Pavlo Tomljenovich × Thomaa»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YJN2. Same household as Josephus 1784, same caveat
Matthæam Tomljenovich||daughter of a DIFFERENT Paulus Tomljanović of Karlobag|baptism|7 October 1787|Karlobag|Karlobag births, indexed — «Pavlo Tomljenovich × Catharina»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YJVT. Recorded to keep the two apart: this Paulus's wife is Catharina and the other's is Thoma, and both father at Karlobag in 1787, so a daughter of «Paulus Tomljanović» in these years is not automatically the same household
Marija Kosina||daughter of Martin Kosina and Angelika Boras; not in the tree|death|1896|Senj|Senj deaths, indexed — born 1896 and BURIED 1896, «Martin Kosina × Angjelina Kosina»; ark 1:1:6B47-LG4G. An infant death the tree does not have, in the same year as Josip below
Josip Kosina||son of Martin Kosina and Angelika Boras; not in the tree|death|1896|Senj|Senj deaths, indexed — born 1896 and BURIED 1896, «Martin Kosina × Angjelina Kosina»; ark 1:1:6B47-LGH2. The second infant of this household to die in 1896; with Marija they are probably twins, which the register would say and the index does not
Petar Kasuniž||father of Anka Kasunić, who married Antun Kosina (1891-1925)|named as parent|1891|Senj|Senj marriages, indexed — named as the bride's father at «Antun Kosina × Anka Kasuniž»; ark 1:1:X9D5-MWF2
Marija Turina||mother of Anka Kasunić, who married Antun Kosina (1891-1925)|named as parent|1891|Senj|Senj marriages, indexed — named as the bride's mother in the same entry; ark 1:1:X9D5-MWF2
Franjo "Frajno" Kosina||possible brother of Pavao Kosina, unplaced|arrival|1 April 1947|Buenos Aires|CEMLA, Buenos Aires port arrivals - "KOSINA FRAJNO, 47, C, CROATA (HRVATSKA), AGRONOMO, 1947/04/01, PHILIPPA, GENOVA". FRAJNO is FRANJO; born about 1900, married, an AGRONOMIST. He sailed from Genoa on the SAME SHIP as Oskar Kosina six months before him. Martin Kozina and Angjelika Boras had sons in 1891 and 1894 and she died in 1902, so a son born about 1900 is possible and NOT established. Nothing joins him to the tree
Gerko Kosina||unplaced, head of a family of six|arrival|10 April 1911|Buenos Aires|CEMLA - "KOSINA GERKO, 30, C, AUSTRIACO - DALMATA, PRIVATO, 1911/04/10, SOFIA HOHENBERG, TRIESTE", with CLARA 25 and four children: ANKA 4, IRMA 4, OJESKOSLAIO 2 and GELKA 0. GERKO is JERKO and OJESKOSLAIO is VJEKOSLAV; the two four-year-olds are twins or one age is wrong. Croatian given names, Austrian-Adriatic nationality, sailing from Trieste. NOT joined to this family and there is nothing but the surname
Ivan Kosina||unplaced, NOT Oskar's son|arrival|30 November 1928|Buenos Aires|CEMLA - "KOSINA IVAN, 27, S, YUGOSLAVA/S.H.S., VELIC, AGRICULTOR, 1928/11/30, GRAL. BELGRANO, HAMBURGO". Born about 1901 and single. He is NOT Ivan Christian, Oskar's son, who was born in Argentina after October 1947 - the archive checked because the names collide
Gertraud "Gertruda" Kosina||MOTHER OF MARTIN KOZINA - not in the tree at all|baptism|18 March 1814|župnija Kranj-Šmartin, house 10|Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1831, book p.28 - "den 18. Merz, Haus 10, Gertrud, ehelich, Vater: FRANZ KOSINAR, Hueblar, Mutter: MARIA DO[M]SHAN". She was 27 when she bore Martin. HER BROTHER IS JOHANN: his marriage of 6 January 1833 gives his father as "Franz Kosinar, Haeusler" and his mother as "Mina Tom[sh]shan, Haeuslerin" - the same couple. RETRACTION: on 21 September 2026 this entry was ELIMINATED here on the grounds that the surname "ends in a clear -r, so it is KOSNAR not Kosina". That was wrong. The -r is how THIS clerk writes the family name, and he writes it identically for Johann, whose own children are entered KOSINA by the next clerk. One family, two hands. HER DEATH, read 22 September 2026: Mrliska knjiga Kranj-Smartin 1870-1890, book p.69 - "5. - 7. [Marec 1880] · Zg. Bitno · 9 · JERA KOZINA, neomozena gostja · katolik · zenski · ALTER 65 let · bozjast in jetika · M. Zarnik". DIED 5 MARCH 1880, BURIED 7 MARCH, AGED 65, UNMARRIED, AT ZGORNJE BITNO 9 - THE HOUSE SHE BORE MARTIN IN. JERA is the Slovene short form of GERTRUDA. Baptised 18 March 1814, she died THIRTEEN DAYS SHORT OF HER SIXTY-SIXTH BIRTHDAY, so the clerk's 65 is exact. NEOMOZENA - never married, which is what the unehelich on Martin's baptism already said. GOSTJA - a lodger, the word for a woman living in a house that is not hers, in the house her brother Johann held. The cause is "bozjast in jetika": the falling sickness and consumption. RETRACTION, THE SAME DAY: this row said for two hours that SHE LEFT THE PARISH, on the grounds that her son's Senj marriage of January 1888 carries no dagger against her name. She had been dead eight years. An absent mark is not a record. Found by reading the 1870-1890 register opening by opening after the 1890-1911 one had given nothing. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00885 image 15, sig. 00899 image 37, sig. 03916 image 72, sig. 03917 read in full
Ursula "Uršula" Sedej||SECOND WIFE of Johann Kozina - and she held the house after him|second marriage|28 May 1873|Zgornje Bitno 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1856-1881 book p.54, entry of 28 May 1873 - "Ženin: ZGORNJE BITNO 72 · MARTIN BRENK, gost · katoliško · 48 · VDOVEC. NEVESTA: ZGORNJE BITNO 9 · URŠULA SEDEJ, PO RANJCIM MOŽU KOZINA, POSESTNICA · katoliško · 46 · VDOVA. Roditelja ženinova: ANTON BRENK, gruntar, in MARIA RAVNIKAR. RODITELJA NEVESTINA: ANDREJ SEDEJ, GRUNTAR NA NOVI OSLICI, in JERA ROJE. Priči: Janez Bašar, kajžar, and Lorenc Brenk, gruntar, both signing with a cross. Oznanjeno Stražišče 27. aprila 1873. Poročil Valentin Lah, kaplan". FOUR THINGS THIS ENTRY GIVES, AND THE ARCHIVE HAD NONE OF THEM. ONE, HER AGE: 46 in May 1873, so BORN ABOUT 1826-27. She was about 27 when Franziska was born in 1853 and about 33 at Maria in 1859, which fits. TWO, HER PARENTS: ANDREJ SEDEJ and JERA ROJE - a generation nobody had reached. THREE, WHERE SHE CAME FROM: her father is a gruntar NA NOVI OSLICI - Nova Oselica, in the Poljane valley south-west of Škofja Loka, twenty-five kilometres from Bitnje and IN ANOTHER PARISH. This archive had already concluded she came from outside Kranj-Šmartin, because her marriage to Johann is not in its register between April 1850 and February 1853; the conclusion was right and this names the place. FOUR, WHAT SHE WAS BY 1873: POSESTNICA - a property owner - AT ZGORNJE BITNO 9. Johann died in October 1868 a Häubler; five years later HIS WIDOW HOLDS THE HOUSE IN HER OWN NAME. AND IT SETTLES SOMETHING THIS ARCHIVE COULD NOT EXPLAIN. At her daughter Mina’s marriage in 1883 the bride is "gruntarska hči" and Janez Kozina "gruntar", which contradicted every other record of a man who was a kajžar all his life. HER FATHER WAS A GRUNTAR AND SHE WAS A POSESTNICA. The household had risen, and by 1883 the clerk was writing what it had become rather than what Johann had been. SHE REMARRIED A WIDOWER, Martin Brenk, a gost of Zgornje Bitno 72, five years after Johann died. Matricula, NSAL sig. 03918 image 55
Andrej Sedej||FATHER of Ursula Sedej - a GRUNTAR at Nova Oselica, and a generation nobody had reached|named as parent|1873|Nova Oselica, Poljane valley|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1856-1881 book p.54 - at his daughter’s second marriage on 28 May 1873 the bride’s parents are entered "ANDREJ SEDEJ, GRUNTAR NA NOVI OSLICI" and "JERA ROJE". A GRUNTAR is a full peasant farmer, a rung above the kajžar his daughter married. NOVA OSELICA is in the Poljane valley south-west of Škofja Loka, some twenty-five kilometres from Zgornje Bitnje AND IN ANOTHER PARISH - which is why Ursula’s first marriage is not in the Kranj-Šmartin book, and where her baptism of about 1826-27 should be. NOVA OSELICA HAS NOW BEEN OPENED, 28 September 2026, and SEDEJ IS A REAL, RESIDENT FAMILY THERE - walking the baptismal register (sig. 01584, 1826-1862) and the marriage register (sig. 01590, 1826-1908) turned up GERTRAUD SEDEJ and CATHARINA SEDEJ as mothers of brides marrying in January 1827, AGNES SEDEJ standing godmother in the same years, and an ANDRE SEDEJ, "½ Hüblor", fathering a child with MARIA BRIZ about 1829-30 (sig. 01584 image 14). NONE OF THESE IS PROVED TO BE THIS ANDREJ. The 1873 marriage names his wife JERA ROJE, not Maria Briz - so either this is a different Andre Sedej of the same generation, or Maria Briz was an earlier wife who died before Ursula was born (the pattern this archive has now met twice, at Johann Kozina’s own house). THE BAPTISMAL WALK COVERED SIG. 01584 IMAGES 3-25 (1826 to about 1832) AND DID NOT FIND URSULA’S OWN ENTRY, nor an Andrej Sedej x Jera Roje pairing as parents. The marriage register 01589 (1785-1826) was checked at its final pages (images 38-44, 1824 to January 1826) and 01590 from its start (images 1-8, 1826-1828): no Andrej Sedej x Jera Roje marriage in either window. EITHER THEIR MARRIAGE OR URSULA’S BAPTISM IS ELSEWHERE IN THESE 99 AND 87 IMAGES, most of which have not been read, or their marriage is in the earlier volume 01588 (1763-1784) or 01583 (1785-1826, the baptismal volume before 01584). NOT PROVED, AND NOT FALSE - the parish is confirmed open and free, and the next session can pick up exactly where this one stopped. Matricula, NSAL sig. 03918 image 55, sig. 01584 images 3-25, sig. 01589 images 38-44, sig. 01590 images 1-8
Jera Roje||MOTHER of Ursula Sedej - named once, at her daughter’s second wedding|named as parent|1873|Nova Oselica, Poljane valley|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1856-1881 book p.54 - "Roditelja nevestina: Andrej Sedej, gruntar na novi Oslici, in JERA ROJE". JERA is the Slovene short form of GERTRUDA, the same name Martin Kozina’s mother carried at Zgornje Bitno 9 - a coincidence of given names in one parish and nothing more. NOVA OSELICA WAS OPENED FOR HER ON 28 September 2026 and did not give her up. The baptismal register (sig. 01584) and the start of the marriage register (sig. 01590) were walked for 1826-1832 and 1826-1828 and neither carries a Jera Roje beside an Andrej Sedej. AN ANDRE SEDEJ DOES APPEAR, married to MARIA BRIZ, fathering a child about 1829-30 - not proved to be the same man, and if it is, Jera Roje is a second wife the walk has not yet reached. SHE STILL EXISTS IN THIS ARCHIVE IN SIX WORDS. The volumes that would settle it - 01584 beyond image 25, 01589 before image 38, 01590 beyond image 8, and the two volumes before them both - are open, free, and not yet read past the pages named here. AND THE SURNAME ITSELF IS NOW INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMED, separately from her husband’s family. Krstna knjiga Nova Oselica 1826-1862 (sig. 01584), image 36, gives an entry naming the mother "AGNES ROJ[S]KA" - the adjectival feminine form Slovene registers give a woman surnamed ROJE, exactly as this clerk’s contemporaries write "Kajzarska" for a woman of the Kajzar house. SO ROJE, LIKE SEDEJ, IS A REAL SURNAME IN THIS SAME PARISH AND NOT A MISREADING. Not the same woman as Jera - this Agnes bore a child outside marriage, later legitimised, a different case entirely - but it means the 1873 marriage record’s "Jera Roje" is not an isolated, unverifiable name: both halves of it belong to Nova Oselica. Matricula, NSAL sig. 03918 image 55, sig. 01584 images 3-36, sig. 01590 images 1-8
Andre Sedej and Maria Briz||a Sedej household at Nova Oselica fathering children about 1829-30 - possibly Andrej and an earlier wife|named as parent|about 1829-1830|Nova Oselica, Poljane valley|Krstna knjiga Nova Oselica 1826-1862 (sig. 01584), image 14 - "ANDRE SEDEJ, ½ Hüblor" named as father, "MARIA BRIZ" as mother, in an entry the archive’s own year-heading dates to 1829 or 1830. FOUND WHILE WALKING THE REGISTER FOR URSULA SEDEJ’S OWN BAPTISM (found.psv, her row). THE WIFE’S NAME DOES NOT MATCH: Ursula’s mother in 1873 is JERA ROJE. Two readings are open and neither is settled - this is a DIFFERENT Andrej Sedej of the same generation and parish, or MARIA BRIZ IS A FIRST WIFE who died before Jera Roje married him, exactly the pattern this archive has already documented once, at Johann Kozina’s own house forty kilometres away. NOTHING HERE PROVES EITHER. ½ Hüblor is a half-cottager, a smaller holding than the GRUNTAR Ursula’s father is called in 1873, which is some evidence against the identification unless the household rose in the years between, which is exactly what this archive found at Zgornje Bitnje 9 as well. Matricula, NSAL sig. 01584 image 14
Johann Kosina||BROTHER OF GERTRAUD, Haeusler at Oberfeichting No. 9|marriage|6 January 1833|Zgornje Bitnje (Oberfeichting) 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1816-1855, book p.35 - "1833, 6. Jaenner, Obern feichting 9, JOHANN KOSINAR, Haeusler, katholisch, 30 Jahre, ledig" marrying "LUZIA LABORNIK, 38, ledig". HIS PARENTS: "Franz Kosinar, Haeusler" and "Mina Tom[sh]shan, Haeuslerin". Born about 1802-03. THE BRIDE IS THE PROOF: Johann Kosina, Haeusler of Oberfeichting 9, had his first child with Lucia Labornik on 20 January 1834, a year and a fortnight later - so the house, the trade, the wife and the date all agree and the identification does not rest on the surname at all. Children ANTON 1834 and PETRUS 1836 at Oberfeichting 9 by Lucia Labornik; then, by a second wife URSULA SEDEJ, three daughters whose days are now all read: FRANZISKA baptised 19 September 1853, ANNA born and baptised 25 July 1856, MARIA born and baptised 7 August 1859 - six children over twenty-five years in one house, and he was about sixty-one at the last of them. CORRECTED 27 September 2026: this row said FRANZ 1853. The register says FRANCISCA and ticks Maedchen. And MARIA 1859 is new - the K section of the baptismal index was read end to end that day and it holds SIX Kozina, not five. HIS DEATH, found 27 September 2026 at the end of the walk that the index had made necessary: Mrliska knjiga Kranj-Smartin 1836-1869 book p.167 - "1868, October · 10. gestorben, 12. begraben · ZGORNJE BITNO · 9 · JOHANN KOZINA, Haubler · katholisch · maennlich · ALTER 64 Jahre · Auszehrung". DIED 10 OCTOBER 1868, BURIED 12 OCTOBER, AGED 64, AT ZGORNJE BITNO 9 - the Slovene name for Oberfeichting, and the same house. Age 64 puts his birth at about 1804 against the 30 he gave at his marriage in January 1833, which gives 1802-03: a two-year spread, which is what register ages do. He is a HAUBLER to the end, the word he carried at his wedding thirty-five years earlier. THE INDEX FOR 1836-1869 DOES NOT LIST HIM, and he is the seventh of the nine Kozina in that register that it missed. HE IS NAMED ONE LAST TIME, FIFTEEN YEARS AFTER HE DIED: at his daughter Maria’s marriage of 1883 (sig. 03919 book p.14) the bride’s parents are entered "JANEZ KOZINA, GRUNTAR, in URŠA SEDEJ" - the Slovene forms of his name and his second wife’s, and the record that joins the "unplaced" Marija Kozina of Stražišče to this household. THE WORD GRUNTAR DOES NOT FIT HIM and is recorded as read: he is a Häubler at his wedding in 1833, a Hüblar at every baptism, and a Häubler at his death in 1868. HIS SECOND MARRIAGE IS NOT IN THIS PARISH, and that was read rather than assumed. Lucia Labornik died 30 November 1850; Franziska was baptised 19 September 1853 and entered EHELICH, so the marriage to Ursula Sedej falls between those dates. Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1816-1855 was walked for it on 28 September 2026 - book pages 66, 67, 68, 69, 70 and 71, which run from APRIL 1850 to FEBRUARY 1853 without a gap. THERE IS NO KOZINA MARRIAGE ON ANY OF THEM. AND THE LIKELIEST REASON IS THE ORDINARY RULE: a marriage is celebrated in the BRIDE’S parish. Johann’s first marriage is in this book because LUCIA LABORNIK was local. If URSULA SEDEJ was not, the entry - and both sets of parents with it - is in her parish’s book and not in this one. SO URSULA SEDEJ CAME FROM SOMEWHERE ELSE, on the evidence of where her marriage is not. HIS TWO SONS’ BAPTISMS, OPENED IN FULL 28 September 2026, and they gave a household the archive had not seen. ANTON: "20. Jänner [1834] · Oberfeichting · 9 · ANTON · katholisch · Knaben · ehelich · Vater: JOHANN KOSINA, Häubler · Mutter: LUCIA · Paten: STEPHAN SH[E]SNAR, Hüblar, and MARIA DOLLENZ". PETRUS: "29. Juni [1836] · Oberfeichting · 9 · PETRUS · katholisch · Knaben · ehelich · Vater: [Johann] KOSINA · Mutter: LUCIA LABORNIK, written in full · Pate: JAKOB DOLENZ, signing with a cross". THE MOTHER’S SURNAME AT PETRUS’S BAPTISM IS THE CONFIRMATION - until now Lucia Labornik was known from her marriage and her death, and the two boys were hers only by inference from the house. AND THE GODPARENTS ARE A FINDING OF THEIR OWN. A DOLENC STANDS AT FOUR BAPTISMS OF THIS HOUSEHOLD ACROSS FORTY-ONE YEARS: JAKOB DOLLENZ in 1812 at Elisabeth’s, MARIA DOLLENZ in 1834 at Anton’s, JAKOB DOLENZ in 1836 at Petrus’s, and MARINA DOLENC in 1853 at Francisca’s. Jakob appears in 1812 and again in 1836, twenty-four years apart - one man, or a father and a son. KUMSTVO IS NOT A COURTESY in this culture; it is a standing bond between two households, and this is the only one this archive has documented for the Kosinar. IT ALSO GIVES A SURNAME TO SEARCH: a Dolenc marriage at Kranj-Šmartin would say how close the two families were. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00899 images 37 and 69-74, sig. 00886 images 19 and 34, sig. 03919 image 15
Lucia Labornik||first wife of Johann Kosina|death|30 November 1850|Zgornje Bitnje (Oberfeichting) 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Mrliska knjiga Kranj-Smartin 1836-1869, book p.71 - "30. - 2. Xbr [1850] · Ob. Feichtg · 9 · LUZIA KOSINA, Hueblersweib · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 55 · Lungenentzuendung · versehen · Jos. Kartely". DIED 30 NOVEMBER 1850, BURIED 2 DECEMBER, AGED 55, so born about 1795 - and she was 38 at her marriage in January 1833, which gives 1794-95. THE SAME WOMAN. She is entered a Hueblers-WEIB and not a widow, which is right: Johann outlived her. AND IT EXPLAINS THE SECOND WIFE - Johann is beside Ursula Sedej by 1853 because Lucia died in 1850. Married 6 January 1833 aged 38 to Johann Kosina, Haeusler of Oberfeichting 9 (Porocna knjiga 1816-1855 p.35); her parents "Ma[thes] Labornik, Haeusler" and "Gertraud Mag[nishan]"; mother of Anton 1834 and Petrus 1836. SAME HOUSE AND SAME DISEASE AS FRANZ, twenty-two months apart. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00899 image 37 and sig. 00895 image 72
Franz Kosinar||GRANDFATHER OF MARTIN KOZINA - father of Gertraud and Johann|death|22 January 1849|Feichting bei St. Johann 10, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1780-1815, read 22 September 2026 - "Den 27ten [8ber 1800] · Feichting b. St. Joh. · 10. · FRANZ KOSINAR · katholisch · 24 · ledig" marrying "MARIA DORTSHEN · katholisch · 20 · ledig". Witnesses "MATTHAEUS KOSINAR" and "Simon Rauth", Bauern, Matthaeus signing with a cross; married by "Matthaeus Lauts, coop.", Pfarrer St. Martin. SO HE WAS BORN ABOUT 1776 and she about 1780. Named again as "Franz Kosinar, Hueblar" at his daughter GERTRAUD's baptism, 18 March 1814 at HOUSE 10 (sig. 00885 image 15), and as "Franz Kosinar, Haeusler" in the Aeltern des Braeutigams column at his son JOHANN's marriage of 6 January 1833 (sig. 00899 image 37). He is Martin Kozina's grandfather, four generations above Hedviga. HIS OWN BAPTISM WAS LOOKED FOR ON 27 SEPTEMBER 2026 AND IS NOT IN THE INDEX. The baptismal index for 1603-1779 (sig. 04.. 00872, 146 images) is arranged by initial letter and then CHRONOLOGICALLY, giving surname, given name, the FATHER in brackets and a date - and no page number, so it finds a date and not a page. The K section runs to about image 72, where it ends at 1779. Images 71 and 72 were read in full at 3.2x and cover 1772 to 1779 without a gap. THERE IS NO FRANZ KOSINAR OR KOSINA IN 1774, 1775, 1776 OR 1777 - the window his two independent ages require (24 at his marriage in October 1800, 73 at his death in January 1849, both giving 1775-76). THAT IS NOT A CONCLUSION AND THIS ARCHIVE HAS BEEN BURNED BY TREATING IT AS ONE. An index proves what it contains and never what it omits, and this parish’s own death index for 1836-1869 missed NINE Kozina. The register itself (sig. 00883, 363 images) has NOT been walked for those four years, and until it is, "not in the index" is all this says. THE OTHER READING is that he was baptised in another parish and married in, which the 1800 marriage does not say either way. HIS DEATH, read 22 September 2026: Mrliska knjiga Kranj-Smartin 1836-1869 book p.61 - "22. - 24. [Jaenner 1849] · Ob. Feichtg · 9 · FRANZ KOSINA, Ausnehmer · katholisch · maennlich · ALTER 73 · Lungenentzuendung · versehen". DIED 22 JANUARY 1849, BURIED 24 JANUARY, AGED 73 - which puts his birth at 1775-76 and CONFIRMS the age of 24 he gave at his marriage, from a second and independent record. He is an AUSNEHMER, a retired householder living on the Ausnahm, and he died at OBERFEICHTING No. 9. CORRECTED 22 September 2026: this row said he had 'retired into his son's house'. HOUSE 9 WAS HIS OWN. His son Valentin was baptised there on 15 February 1820 with Franz entered HAUBLER, the man of the house (sig. 00885 image 55), and Elisabeth was baptised at house 9 in 1812. He held 9, his son Johann was keeping it by 1833, his grandson MARTIN WAS BORN IN IT in 1841, and he died in it as an Ausnehmer in 1849. He did not move in with his son; he handed the house over and stayed in it. The family were at house 10 in 1814-15 and at 9 before and after, so the two numbers are a move and not two households. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00901 image 33 and sig. 00895 image 62
Maria "Mina" Dortschen||GRANDMOTHER OF MARTIN KOZINA - wife of Franz Kosinar|marriage|27 October 1800|Feichting bei St. Johann, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga 1780-1815 - "MARIA DORTSHEN, katholisch, 20, ledig", marrying Franz Kosinar on 27 October 1800, SO BORN ABOUT 1780. THE SURNAME, from six clerks across thirty-three years: "Dortshen" 1800 · "Dortschen" at Elisabeth's baptism 1812 · "Do[m]shan" at Gertraud's 1814 · "Dortschen" at Maria's 1815 · "Dortschen" at Valentin's 1820 · "Tom[sh]shan" at Johann's marriage 1833. FOUR OF THE SIX READ DORTSCHEN and the archive now leads with it; the other two are this archive's own bracketed readings and are kept as read. MINA is the short form these registers use for Marija, and one clerk writes MARINA. SIX OF HER CHILDREN ARE NOW KNOWN BY NAME: Johann about 1802, Elisabeth 1812, Gertraud 1814, Maria 1815, MARIA 1818 and Valentin 1820 - and THREE OF THE SIX died before they were a year old. THE SECOND MARIA, read 22 September 2026, is named for the sister who had died in March 1816, which is ordinary practice and is why this archive counted five for part of one evening and then six. Two index entries were long unaccounted for - Kosina Dorothea p.8 (1813) and Kosina Marianna p.16 (1813). CORRECTED 27 September 2026: this row said BOTH PAGES WERE OPENED and the whole father column of each read at 2.4x, and that THERE IS NO KOSINA ON EITHER. THAT WAS WRONG FOR PAGE 16. Re-read at nine times magnification, the entry of 12 August 1813 at house 27 gives MARIANNA, father LUKAS KOSINER, Kaischler - and she is almost certainly the Marianna Kosina who died at Breg 12 in 1840 aged 26. Two and a half times was not enough for that hand. CORRECTED AGAIN THE SAME DAY, AND FOR THE SAME REASON. For an hour this row also said PAGE 8 STILL HAS NO KOSINA, on the strength of a 3.2x pass that found two Dorotheas - house 28 to Primus Wit[nitz] and house 18 to Johann Holz. THERE ARE THREE DOROTHEAS ON PAGE 8. The third is "6. [Hornung 1813] · 12 · DOROTHEA · ehelich · Vater: ANTON KOSINER RECTE KATZIN, Inwohner · Mutter: MARGARETH ZUBERTH". The whole father column has now been read at 8x and she is the only Kosiner on it. BOTH INDEX ENTRIES ARE THEREFORE ACCOUNTED FOR - and NEITHER CHILD IS HERS: Marianna is Lukas Kosina’s, and Dorothea is Anton’s. AND ANTON’S ENTRY CARRIES A WARNING FOR THIS WHOLE FILE: RECTE marks the legal surname against the name in daily use, so the family name is KATZIN and KOSINER is what they were called - most likely after the house. A Kosina in this index is not always a Kosina in the family. SHE WAS ALIVE IN FEBRUARY 1820, at about forty, because Valentin was baptised then and entered ehelich. HER DEATH IS STILL NOT FOUND, and the search is now exhaustive for this parish: the K section of the death index for 1812-1835 (sig. 04634, images 125-126) was read end to end on 22 September 2026 and holds SIX Kozina - Elisabeth 1813 p.6, TWO Maria 1816 both p.34, Matthäus 1819 p.64, Valentin 1820 p.72, Margareth 1826 p.132 - and the two 1816 Marias are a woman of 78 and a baby of nine months, NEITHER of them her. The index for 1836-1869 (sig. 04635) holds only Franz 1849 and Luzia 1850. HER DEATH, FOUND 27 SEPTEMBER 2026 by walking the 1836-1869 register itself rather than trusting its index: Mrliska knjiga Kranj-Smartin 1836-1869 book p.27 - "1841, April · am 11. gestorben, am 13. begraben · OBERFEICHTING [ditto] · 9 · MARIA KOSINA, AUSZUGLERIN · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 60 Jahre · Convulsionen · versehen". DIED 11 APRIL 1841, BURIED 13 APRIL, AGED 60, AT OBERFEICHTING 9. Born about 1781, which is the 20 she gave at her marriage in October 1800. AUSZUGLERIN is the female of AUSNEHMER - a householder who has handed over and lives on the Ausnahm - and it is the exact word this same register uses for FRANZ at his own death in THE SAME HOUSE eight years later (p.61, 22 January 1849, aged 73). SHE DIED IN THE HOUSE SHE HAD HANDED OVER. AND THE DATE IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS: her grandson MARTIN WAS BORN IN THAT HOUSE ON 16 NOVEMBER 1841, SEVEN MONTHS AFTER SHE DIED IN IT. THE INDEX FOR 1836-1869 DOES NOT LIST HER, and that is now the fourth positive proof that it is incomplete - it holds Franz 1849 and Luzia 1850 and nobody else, while the register itself yields Marianna 1840, MARIA 1841, Joseph 1843 and Ursula 1845/46 in the first 105 pages alone. An index proves what it contains and never what it omits. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00901 image 33, sig. 00885 images 4, 15, 23 and 55, sig. 00899 image 37
Matthaeus Kosinar||witness at Franz Kosinar's marriage - and his DEATH says brother, not father|death|16 April 1819|Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje) 14, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1780-1815 - one of the two Beystände at the marriage of Franz Kosinar and Maria Dortschen on 27 October 1800, entered "MATTHAEUS KOSINAR" and SIGNING WITH A CROSS, so he could not write. The other witness is "Simon Rauth"; both are entered "Bauern". HIS DEATH, read 22 September 2026: Mrliška knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1835 book p.64 - "1819, den 16ten April · Ober-Feichting · 14 · MATTHÄUS KOSINA · Keischler · katholisch · männlich · ALTER 45 · Rothlauf und Brand". DIED 16 APRIL 1819, AGED 45, so born about 1774 - WHICH ANSWERS THE OPEN QUESTION. Franz was born 1775-76. Two men born a year or two apart are not father and son, so the man who stood witness in 1800 was FRANZ'S BROTHER and was twenty-six when he did it. He is the only Matthäus Kozina in the parish death index for 1812-1835. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00901 image 33 and sig. 00894 image 33
Lukas Kosina the elder||A KOSINA FATHERING CHILDREN 1773-1779 - the candidate father of Franz, Matthaeus and Lukas|named as parent|1773 and 1779|župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Krstni index Kranj-Šmartin 1603-1779, the K section, read 27 September 2026 - TWO ENTRIES: "KOSINA GERTRUD (Lukas) 2.3." under 1773, and "KOSINA HELENA (Lukas) 26.4." under 1779. The index gives the FATHER in brackets and a date, and no page, so these are two daughters of a LUKAS KOSINA baptised six years apart. HE CANNOT BE THE LUKAS THIS ARCHIVE ALREADY HAS. That Lukas married in 1799 aged 29, so he was born about 1770 and was three years old when Gertrud was baptised. THIS IS AN OLDER MAN OF THE SAME NAME, fathering children at Kranj-Šmartin from 1773. AND THAT IS EXACTLY THE GENERATION THIS ARCHIVE HAS BEEN SHORT OF. Its three earliest Kosina men are MATTHAEUS born about 1774, FRANZ born 1775-76 and LUKAS born about 1770 - three men born inside six years, whom the archive has only ever been able to call brothers on the arithmetic of their ages. A Lukas Kosina fathering children in 1773 and 1779 is a candidate for their father, and the 1773 and 1779 girls would be their sisters. NOTHING PROVES IT. No entry yet read names Lukas the elder’s wife, his house or his village, and the two baptisms have NOT been opened - the index carries no page number and the register (sig. 00883) has not been walked to find them. THE TEST IS THE HOUSE: if either girl is baptised at Oberfeichting 9, the house Franz held and died in, the case is made; if neither is, it is not. THE REST OF THE K SECTION, 1747 to 1772, HAS NOT BEEN READ, so there may be more of them. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00872 images 71 and 72
Lukas Kosina||married 1799 aged 29 - father of the OTHER Gertraud, and not ours|marriage|1799|župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1780-1815 - "LUKAS KOSINA, katholisch, 29, ledig", married in 1799, so born about 1770. HE CLOSES AN OPEN QUESTION: the 1812-1831 baptismal index offered TWO Gertraud candidates, and the 1818 one (book p.72, house 12) had a father whose surname could not be read - "Lukas Ko[s]in..." - at the resolution Matricula serves. This is that man. The 1818 Gertraud is HIS daughter and not Franz's, which leaves the 1814 Gertraud as Martin's mother with no rival. HIS CHILDREN, 27 September 2026: TWO are now named, and his surname is no longer unreadable. Book p.16 gives MARIANNA, baptised 12 August 1813 at house 27, and book p.72 gives GERTRAUD, baptised 16 February 1818 at "Lemny" house 12 - the village as the clerk wrote it, not resolved. BOTH entries name the father LUKAS KOSINER, Kaischler, and both name the mother LUZIA; her surname is written differently in the two hands and neither reading is secure. At fourteen times magnification the surname is KOSINER on both, which is how these clerks write this family name - Franz is KOSINAR and KOSINER in the same decades. AND THE 1813 DAUGHTER IS ALMOST CERTAINLY THE MARIANNA KOSINA who died at BREG 12 on 10 January 1840, aged 26, a Keuschlerstochter: the age fits to the month and the trade is the same word. HIS VILLAGE, 27 September 2026: READ CLEANLY TWICE AND STILL NOT IDENTIFIED. The 1799 marriage puts him at "LEMY 37" and the 1818 baptism of his daughter Gertraud at "LEMNY 12" - the same short name in two hands nineteen years apart, and the column header of the 1818 page is "DER ORTEN", so it is a place and not anything else. At thirteen times magnification the 1799 form is four letters, a kurrent capital L, then e or o, then m, then y. IT MATCHES NO SETTLEMENT IN THE PARISH LIST Matricula publishes - but that list is NOT EXHAUSTIVE, because the same 1818 page carries "PRSCHAN" for Prase, which is not in it either. So the likeliest answer is a hamlet too small for a summary list, and this is a question for somebody who knows the ground rather than for more magnification. AND THERE IS ONE HYPOTHESIS WITH A NUMBER BEHIND IT. Lukas is at Lemny 12 in 1818; his daughter MARIANNA dies at BREG 12 in 1840. THE SAME HOUSE NUMBER, the same family, twenty-two years apart. Either the household moved from one village 12 to another village 12, which happens, or LEMY IS A PART OF BREG under a name the clerks used and the gazetteers do not. THE WORDS DO NOT RESEMBLE EACH OTHER, which is the weakness of it, and this archive is not going to turn a house number into a place name. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00901 image 31, sig. 00885 images 9 and 37
Elisabeth Kosinar||DAUGHTER of Franz Kosinar and Maria Dortschen - died at five months|baptism and death|baptised 18 November 1812, died 11 April 1813|Oberfeichting bei St. Ursula 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|BAPTISM: Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1831 book p.6 - "18. [November 1812] · Haus 9 · ELISABETH · katholisch · weiblich · ehelich · Vater: FRANZ KOSINER · Mutter: MINA DORTSCHEN · Paten Jakob Dollenz and Elisabeth, signing with a cross · den 18ten um 3 Uhr früh". DEATH: Mrliška knjiga 1812-1835 book p.6 - "11. [April 1813] · Ober-Feichting W. Ursula · 9 · ELIZABETHA KOSINA · Tochter · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 5 Monath · Fraiß". FIVE MONTHS OLD, of convulsions. She is the first of the three children of this marriage the archive has found who did not live. Indexed as "Kosina Elisabeth 6" in BOTH the baptismal index 1812-1831 and the death index 1812-1835. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00885 image 4, sig. 00894 image 4, sig. 04631 image 169, sig. 04634 image 125
Maria Kosinar||DAUGHTER of Franz Kosinar and Maria Dortschen - died at nine months|baptism and death|baptised 8 August 1815, died 31 March 1816|house 10, died at Oberfeichting 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|BAPTISM: Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1831 book p.44 - "den 8ten [August 1815] · Haus 10 · MARIA · katholisch · weiblich · ehelich · Vater: FRANZ KOSINAR, Häubler · Mutter: MARIA DORTSCHEN · um 10 Uhr Nachmittag". DEATH: Mrliška knjiga 1812-1835 book p.34 - "den 31 [März 1816] · Oberfeichting · 9 · MARIA KOZINAR · Häubl[erskind] · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 3/4 Jahr · Fraiß". Born 8 August 1815 and dead on 31 March 1816 is seven and a half months, which is what three quarters of a year means in this column. SHE IS ONE OF THE TWO «Kozina Maria - 34» the death index lists for 1816, and she is the one a reader would be looking for. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00885 image 23, sig. 00894 image 18, sig. 04631 image 169, sig. 04634 image 126
Valentin Kosina||SON of Franz Kosinar and Maria Dortschen - died at one week|baptism and death|baptised 15 February 1820, died 29 February 1820|Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje) 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|BAPTISM: Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1831 book p.108 - "Den 15ten Hornung [February] 1820 · Ober-Feichting · 9 · VALENTIN · katholisch · männlich · ehelich · Vater: FRANZ KOSINA, HÄUBLER · Mutter: MARINA DORTSCHEN". DEATH: Mrliška knjiga 1812-1835 book p.72 - "Den 29ten Hornung · Ober-Feichting · 9 · VALENTIN KOSINA · Häubler · katholisch · männlich · ALTER 1 Woche · Fraiß". Fourteen days. THIS ENTRY IS THE PROOF OF THE HOUSE: it is the only record that names Franz, names Oberfeichting 9 and names him HÄUBLER there, twenty-one years before his grandson Martin was born in that house and twenty-nine before he died in it himself. AND IT DATES THE MOTHER: Maria Dortschen was bearing children in February 1820, so she was alive at about forty. 1820 was a leap year, so the 29th of February is a real date. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00885 image 55, sig. 00894 image 37, sig. 04631 image 169, sig. 04634 image 125
Margaretha Kosinar||a Kosinar woman of Franz's own generation, dying in Franz's house - UNPLACED|death|14 March 1826|Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje) 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Mrliška knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1835 book p.130 - "14. März [1826] · Ober-Feichting · 9 · MARGARETHA KOZINAR · Häublers-Tochter · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 45". BORN ABOUT 1781, and she died UNMARRIED - a Häubler's daughter at forty-five - IN THE HOUSE FRANZ KOSINAR KEPT. Franz was born 1775-76 and Matthäus about 1774, so a woman born about 1781 is of their generation and not of their children's: most likely FRANZ'S SISTER, living on in her brother's house. NOTHING HERE PROVES IT and no parents are named. The death index carries her as "Kozina Margareth - 132", one opening further on than the page she is actually written on, which is the only place this index has been caught out. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00894 image 66, sig. 04634 image 125
Maria Kosinar the elder||a Kosinar woman born about 1738 - the oldest of the name yet reached - UNPLACED|death|27 February 1816|"Zubern" 4, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Mrliška knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1835 book p.34 - "Den 27 [Februar 1816] · Z[ubern] · 4 · MARIA KOZINAR · Häubl · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 78 Jahre · Altersschwäche". SEVENTY-EIGHT, of old age, which puts her birth at about 1738 and makes her the oldest person of this name the archive has reached - a generation above Franz and Matthäus, who were born about 1775 and 1774. She is therefore a CANDIDATE FOR THEIR MOTHER and nothing more: the village is not Feichting, no husband is named, and this book names no parents. THE VILLAGE IS NOT SECURELY READ. It is written the same way twice on this page, house 4 both times, and at 9x it reads "Zubern" or "Luberan"; it is recorded as the clerk wrote it rather than resolved into a modern name. She is the SECOND of the two «Kozina Maria - 34» the index lists for 1816; the other is Franz's nine-month-old daughter. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00894 image 18, sig. 04634 image 126
Maria Kosinar the second||DAUGHTER of Franz Kosinar and Maria Dortschen - named for the sister who died|baptism|6 December 1818|Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje), župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1831 book p.84 - "6ten Dezember [1818] · Ober-Feichting · [10 struck, 12 written] · MARIA · katholisch · weiblich · ehelich · Vater: FRANZ KOSINAR, Häusler · Mutter: MARIA DORTSCHAN, Häuslerin". THE REGISTER CALLS HER SIMPLY MARIA; this archive says "the second" because her sister of the same name had died on 31 March 1816, twenty months before she was born. Re-using a dead child's name is ordinary practice and is not a clerical error. HER HOUSE NUMBER IS CORRECTED ON THE PAGE, 10 struck and 12 written or the reverse - which is the third time these two numbers have moved under this family. Found by reading the K section of the baptismal index 1812-1831 (sig. 04631 image 169), which lists her as "Kosina Maria - 84". HER DEATH, found 27 September 2026: Mrliska knjiga Kranj-Smartin 1836-1869 book p.163 - "1868 · 6. gestorben, 8. begraben · ZGORNJE BITNO · 9 · MARIA KOSINA, LEDIGE INWOHNERIN · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 49 Jahre · Auszehrung · Leopold Plinar, coop.". DIED 6 JANUARY 1868, AGED 49 - and she was baptised 6 DECEMBER 1818, so she had turned 49 exactly one month before she died. THE AGE IS EXACT. LEDIGE: she never married, and she was an INWOHNERIN, a lodger, in the house she was born in. HER SISTER GERTRAUD DIED IN THE SAME HOUSE TWELVE YEARS LATER, also unmarried, also entered as a lodger - «neomozena gostja». TWO SISTERS WHO NEVER LEFT AND NEVER MARRIED, in a house neither of them owned. The index lists neither. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00885 image 43, sig. 04631 image 169
Marija "Mina" Kozina||DAUGHTER of Johann Kozina and Ursula Sedej - the same woman as Maria of 1859, joined on 27 September 2026|marriage|2 July 1883 (see below)|Stražišče, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|THE MARRIAGE, FOUND 27 September 2026 by walking the register this row had named as the document that would settle it: Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1881-1899, sig. 03919, book p.14 - "Ženin: STRAŽIŠE 120 · KANCIJAN ČESEN, kajžarski sin · katoliške · 32 · svoboden. NEVESTA: KOLODVOR V PODNARTU 12, ROJENA V ZGORNJEM BITNJU št. 9 · MINA KOZINA, gruntarska hči · katoliške · 23 · svobodna. Roditelja ženinova: MATEVŽ ČESEN, kajžar, in URŠA PETERNEL. RODITELJA NEVESTINA: JANEZ KOZINA, GRUNTAR, IN URŠA SEDEJ. Priči: Franc Sušnik, hišar, in Jošt Trebar, gostač, both signing with a cross. Poročil Gregor Slibar". TWO THINGS IN THAT ENTRY CLOSE THIS ROW. First, ROJENA V ZGORNJEM BITNJU ŠT. 9 - born at Zgornje Bitnje number 9, which is Franz Kosinar’s house, the house Martin was born in and Johann died in. Second, JANEZ KOZINA and URŠA SEDEJ are the Slovene forms of JOHANN KOZINA and URSULA SEDEJ. SHE IS THEIR YOUNGEST DAUGHTER, baptised 7 August 1859 at that house - and she was 23 at her marriage, which is exact. WHAT THIS ROW USED TO SAY: "the only Kozina woman in the parish in the 1890s, UNPLACED · NOTHING JOINS HER TO THIS FAMILY except the surname and the parish". It named the document that would settle it and said NOT YET OPENED. It has been opened, and it settles it. THE DATE IS A PROBLEM AND IS RECORDED AS ONE. The date cell reads "2. junija" - 2 June 1883 - but the entry’s own Dokaznice are dated 17 June (the Stražišče notice, št. 11), 21 JUNE (the imperial-royal court at Kranj declaring the UNDER-AGE BRIDE of full age, št. 3708) and 1 JULY (the banns from the parish of Dobrava). A marriage cannot precede its own banns by a month, and the row beneath it has the same cell and the same problem, so the month is a slip and the marriage is 2 JULY 1883. Recorded as read, with the conflict stated. AND ONE WORD DOES NOT FIT. She is "gruntarska hči" and her father "gruntar" - a farmer and a farmer’s daughter. Every other record of Johann Kozina calls him Häubler or kajžar, a cottager, including his own death in 1868. Either the household had risen, or the clerk wrote the higher word at a wedding; the birth house and both parents’ names are not in doubt. SHE WAS LIVING AT THE RAILWAY STATION AT PODNART, twenty kilometres from the house she was born in. HER CHILDREN: Mrliška knjiga 1890-1911 gives two of them dying at STRAŽIŠČE 84 - Kancijan, 1892, aged 1 3/4 months, and Pavla, 1893, aged 2 - both "zakonski otrok hišarja-dninarja Kancijana Česen in Marije roj. Kozina". AND THE SAME WALK DATES HER DEATH, WITHOUT FINDING IT. Eleven openings further on, at book p.55: "1896, 10. februarja · STRAŽIŠČE 84 · KANCIJAN ČESEN, hišar, VDOVEC, roj. 1. avgusta 1851, 44 let" marrying "FRANCIŠKA TOMAŽEVIČ, Stražišče 96, kajž. hči, roj. 26. marca 1849, 46 let". HE IS A WIDOWER AT THE HOUSE HER CHILDREN DIED IN. So MARIJA KOZINA DIED BETWEEN 1893, when her daughter Pavla died, and 10 FEBRUARY 1896 - aged between 33 and 36, leaving a husband who remarried within three years. HER DEATH, FOUND 27 September 2026, and the hypothesis that found it was right. Mrliška knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1890-1911 book p.45, entry 33 - "1895, April · 2. umrla, 3. pokopana · STRAŽIŠČE · 84 · MARIJA ČESEN, hišarja in sitarja žena · katoliške · ženskega · STAROST 35 LET · OTROŠKA MRZLICA · previdena · Alojzij Železny, kapelan". DIED 2 APRIL 1895, BURIED 3 APRIL, AGED 35, AT STRAŽIŠČE 84 - the house her children died in. Baptised 7 August 1859, she was 35 years and 8 months. THE AGE IS EXACT. AND SHE IS ENTERED MARIJA ČESEN, UNDER HER HUSBAND’S SURNAME, WITH NO MAIDEN NAME AT ALL. This archive walked that register opening by opening looking for KOZINA and could not have found her. The register is inconsistent about it - on the same openings "Marija roj. Eržen" and "Neža roj. Mravlje" keep their maiden names - so this was not a rule to be known in advance, and the walk was right while the query was wrong. OTROŠKA MRZLICA is childbed fever. For a married woman of thirty-five, among entries where the clerk gives grown people grown diseases, it is not a children’s fever; SHE DIED IN OR JUST AFTER CHILDBIRTH, and a baptism of early 1895 at Stražišče 84 has not been looked for. AND SHE WAS THE FOURTH DEATH IN THAT HOUSE IN THREE YEARS. Kancijan, 1892, at one and three quarter months. Pavla, 1893, at two. ANTONIJA ČESEN, "hišarja hči", 26 FEBRUARY 1895, AGED 1 1/2, of božjast and without the sacraments - born about August 1893, the year Pavla died, and dead FIVE WEEKS BEFORE HER MOTHER. Then Marija herself. Her husband Kancijan Česen remarried on 10 February 1896, ten months later. Matricula, NSAL sig. 03919 images 15 and 56, sig. 00886 image 160, sig. 03917 images 19, 25, 45 and 46 Matricula, NSAL sig. 03919 images 15 and 56, sig. 00886 image 160, sig. 03917 images 19 and 25
Jožef Kozina||head of a KOZINA FARMING household at Kranj-Šmartin in the 1890s - UNPLACED|named as parent|1897|župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1881-1899, book p.59 - at the marriage of IGNACIJ KERT and FRANCIŠKA KOZINA in 1897 the bride’s parents are entered "JOŽEF KOZINA, 1/2 ZEMLJAK" and "MINA KODRAN". HE WAS ALIVE AND HE SIGNED: the Dokaznice column records "Očetovo privoljenje za mladoletno nevesto z dne 5. februarja 1897" - the father’s consent for an under-age bride - so Franciška was not yet twenty-four and was born after about 1873. A 1/2 ZEMLJAK is a half-holding farmer, which is a rung above the Häubler and kajžar this archive’s own Kozina were. NOTHING JOINS HIM TO JOHANN KOZINA of Zgornje Bitnje 9, who died in 1868, and the surname and the parish are the whole resemblance - except that Johann’s daughter is herself entered "gruntarska hči" at her marriage in 1883, which this archive cannot explain. Found by walking the marriage register for somebody else. Matricula, NSAL sig. 03919 image 60
Franciška Kozina, married Kert||DAUGHTER of Jožef Kozina and Mina Kodran - UNPLACED|marriage|1897|župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1881-1899, book p.59 - "IGNACIJ KERT, zemljak" marrying "FRANCIŠKA KOZINA, 1/2 zemljakova hči", his parents the late JOŽEF KERT, zemljak, and JERA JERALA, hers JOŽEF KOZINA, 1/2 zemljak, and MINA KODRAN; witnesses JANEZ JEŠE and ANTON PAPLER, both gruntar. SHE WAS UNDER TWENTY-FOUR and married on her father’s written consent of 5 February 1897, so she was born after about 1873. SHE IS NOT THE FRANZISKA KOZINA OF 1853, who died of measles at eleven in 1864; the two are forty years apart and this archive keeps them apart by their fathers. Nothing joins her to Johann Kozina’s house. Matricula, NSAL sig. 03919 image 60
Urban Kozina||head of a SECOND Kozina farming household, a KMET - UNPLACED|named as parent|1898|župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1881-1899, book p.65 - at the marriage of ANTON ŽIHERL and MARIJA KOZINA in 1898 the bride’s parents are entered "URBAN KOZINA, KMET" and "MARIJANA GORJANC". KMET is a full peasant farmer. AND THE SAME ENTRY CARRIES TWO MORE KOZINA. The groom’s own mother is "MARIJANA KOZINA", already dead, wife of the late Urban Žiherl, kajžar - so a Kozina woman had married into the Žiherl house a generation earlier, and the 1898 marriage is cousins marrying or something near it. And the first witness is "JANEZ KOZINA, gruntarjev sin" - a farmer’s son, most likely the bride’s brother. FOUR KOZINA IN ONE ENTRY, none of them joined to this archive’s line by anything but the surname and the parish. Matricula, NSAL sig. 03919 image 66
Marija Kozina, married Žiherl||DAUGHTER of Urban Kozina and Marijana Gorjanc - UNPLACED|marriage|1898|župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Poročna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1881-1899, book p.65 - "ANTON ŽIHERL, gruntar" marrying "MARIJA KOZINA, gruntarja hči", his parents the late URBAN ŽIHERL, kajžar, and the late MARIJANA KOZINA, hers URBAN KOZINA, kmet, and MARIJANA GORJANC; witnesses JANEZ KOZINA, gruntarjev sin, and ANTON BAJŽELJ, gruntar. HER HUSBAND’S MOTHER WAS ALSO A KOZINA, so she married into a house her own family had already married into once. THE THIRD AND LAST KOZINA BRIDE in the twenty-five years of this volume, and the only one of the three whose father is a full KMET. Nothing joins her to Johann Kozina of Zgornje Bitnje 9. Matricula, NSAL sig. 03919 image 66
Joseph Kosina||infant of the house Martin was born in - almost certainly Johann and Lucia's son|death|27 March 1843|Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje) 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Mrliška knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1836-1869 book p.33 - "1843, März · 27. gestorben · OBERFEICHTING · 9 · JOSEPH KOSINA, Häublers Sohn · katholisch · männlich · ALTER 2 Jahre · Halsentzündung". Born about 1841, DIED AT TWO, AT OBERFEICHTING 9 - the house Johann Kosina held as Häusler from 1833, where Martin was born in November 1841 and where Franz died in 1849. A HÄUBLER'S SON at that house in 1843 is Johann's son, and so a brother of ANTON 1834 and PETRUS 1836. NOT PROVED: this book names no parents. THE COUNT IS NOW SETTLED AND IT DOES NOT HELP HIM. On 27 September 2026 the whole K section of the 1832-1870 baptismal index (sig. 04632, images 246 and 247, entry 1 to entry 369, 1832 to 1870) was read end to end. It holds SIX Kozina and no more: Anton 1834 p.18 - Petrus 1836 p.33 - Martin 1841 p.64 - Francisca 1853 p.130 - Ana 1856 p.144 - MARIA 1859 p.159. The old count of five was short by one, and the one it had missed is MARIA 1859, not Joseph. THERE IS NO JOSEPH IN THAT INDEX. So either he was baptised outside the parish, or this index missed him the way the death index for the same years missed nine Kozina. The second is the likelier of the two on this archive’s own evidence, and neither is proved. Found by walking the register on 27 September 2026; THE INDEX DOES NOT LIST HIM. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00895 image 34
Ursula Kosina||a Kosinar woman born about 1760 who had HELD a THIRD Oberfeichting house - UNPLACED|death|28 March 1845|Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje) 13, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Mrliška knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1836-1869 book p.43 - "1845, März · 28. gestorben, 30. begraben · Ob. Feichting · 13 · URSCHULA KOSINA, ABNEHMERIN · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 85 · Altersschwäche · versehen · idem". EIGHTY-FIVE, of old age, so BORN ABOUT 1760 - a generation above Franz (1775-76) and Matthäus (about 1774), and the second-oldest of the name this archive has reached after the Maria who died at 78 in 1816. AT OBERFEICHTING 13, which is neither Franz’s 9 nor Matthäus’s 14: a THIRD house of the name in one village. THE DATE, COMPLETED 27 September 2026: this row read "28th of a month in 1845 or 1846" for a day, because the month heading sits above the entry and had not been transcribed. The page was re-opened and read from its own head down. The printed year at the top of the column is 1845; the month headings run Jänner (29th), Februar (26th), MäRZ (2nd) - and from there the days run 2, 4, 6, 12, 13, 16, 18, 18, 25, 28, 30 without another heading, the last of them buried "1. April". HERS IS THE 28th, INSIDE MARCH. She died 28 MARCH 1845 and was buried on the 30th. AND THE WORD UNDER HER NAME IS NEW AND IT MATTERS: ABNEHMERIN, read at 10x. It is the female of Abnehmer and it is the same institution as the AUSNEHMER this register calls Franz at his death in 1849 and the AUSZÜGLERIN it calls Maria Dortschen at hers in 1841 - a householder who has HANDED THE HOUSE OVER and lives on the reserved portion. SO SHE HELD OBERFEICHTING 13 AND GAVE IT UP. She is not a lodger and not somebody’s widowed mother taken in: the third Kosina house in this village was HERS. That makes her a stronger candidate for the generation above Franz than the bare age did, and it still does not prove it - no parents, no husband, no children are named here. THE INDEX DOES NOT LIST HER. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00895 image 44
Dorothea Kosiner recte Katzin||the third «Kosina» of 1813 - and the register says the family name is KATZIN|baptism|6 February 1813|house 12, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1831 book p.8 - "6. [Hornung 1813] · 12 · DOROTHEA · katholisch · weiblich · ehelich · Vater: ANTON KOSINER RECTE KATZIN, Inwohner · Mutter: MARGARETH ZUBERTH". SHE IS THE "Kosina Dorothea - 8" the 1812-1831 baptismal index lists under 1813, and she closes the last of the two entries that file had open. THE ENTRY IS A WARNING, WHICH IS WHY SHE HAS A ROW. RECTE marks the LEGAL surname against the name a family is called by, so this household’s name is KATZIN and KOSINER is the by-name - almost certainly the house’s. A KOSINA IN THIS INDEX IS NOT ALWAYS A KOSINA IN THE FAMILY, and this archive has been counting index lines. The alternative reading, that the clerk meant the reverse, is not ruled out; RECTE is written plainly and the direction is the standard one. HER FATHER IS AN INWOHNER - a lodger - at house 12, which is the number Lukas Kosina’s household carries in 1818, so Anton may have been lodging with them; nothing here says so. NOTHING JOINS EITHER OF THEM TO FRANZ KOSINAR’S LINE. HOW SHE WAS FOUND, and it is the second time in one afternoon: this archive published twice that page 8 has no Kosina - once at 2.4x and once at 3.2x - and she is the third Dorothea on a page where two were seen. At 8x the column is plain. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00885 image 5, sig. 04631 image 169
Marianna Kosina||DAUGHTER of Lukas Kosina - baptised 1813, dead at 26 - not in the tree|baptism and death|baptised 12 August 1813, died 10 January 1840|baptised at house 27, died at Breg 12, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|DEATH: Mrliška knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1836-1869 book p.22 - "1840, Jänner · am 10. gestorben, am 12. begraben · BREG · 12 · MARIANNA KOSINA, Keuschlerstochter · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 26 Jahre · Abzehrung · versehen". BAPTISM, FOUND 27 September 2026: Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1812-1831 book p.16 - "12. [August 1813] · Haus 27 · MARIANNA · katholisch · weiblich · ehelich · Vater: LUKAS KOSINER, Kaischler · Mutter: LUZIA O[K]LIN[T]SH". THE MATCH IS THREE THINGS AT ONCE. The age: baptised 12 August 1813, she was 26 years and five months on 10 January 1840, and the clerk wrote 26. The trade: she dies a KEUSCHLERSTOCHTER and her father is entered a KAISCHLER, which is the same word. And the index: the 1812-1831 baptismal index lists "Kosina Marianna - 16" under 1813, and this entry is on book page 16. NOT PROVED - the 1813 entry gives a house number and no village, so it cannot be tied to Breg, and no register yet read joins the two records directly. But it is no longer a guess. SHE IS LUKAS KOSINA’S DAUGHTER, and so a sister of the GERTRAUD he had in 1818 - the Gertraud this archive had to rule out before it could say Martin’s mother was the Gertraud of 1814. THE CORRECTION THIS COST: this archive published that page 16 had been opened and its whole father column read at 2.4x, and that THERE IS NO KOSINA ON IT. There is. Two and a half times magnification was not enough for this hand; at nine times the name is plain. Breg is a fourth Kosina settlement in the parish after Franz’s Oberfeichting 9, Matthäus’s 14 and Ursula’s 13, and she is still born the same year as Gertraud Kozina of Feichting, who lived to 1880 - a reminder that a name and a year together prove nothing. THE 1836-1869 DEATH INDEX DOES NOT LIST HER. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00895 image 23, sig. 00885 image 9, sig. 04631 image 169
Franziska Kozina||DAUGHTER of Johann Kozina and Ursula Sedej - the archive had recorded her as a boy|baptism and death|baptised 19 September 1853, died 7 March 1864|Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje) 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|BAPTISM, read 27 September 2026 on this row’s own instruction: Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1832-1870 book p.130 - "September 19. · Obr. Feichting · 9 · FRANCISCA · katholisch · ehelich · Vater: JOHANN KOZINA, Hüblar · Mutter: URSULA SEDEJ · Paten Johann Pevc and Marina Dolenc". THE SEX COLUMN, WHICH IS WHAT THIS ROW WAS OPENED FOR: the stroke stands in MÄDCHEN and the Knaben cell holds a dot. Read at 8x, and then checked a second way - the tick column was cropped from the printed heading down to her line and counted against all sixteen entries of the page, so the mark is placed by the column it sits under and not by eye. SHE IS A GIRL. DEATH: Mrliška knjiga 1836-1869 book p.140 - "1864, März · 7. gestorben, 9. begraben · OBERNFEICHTING · 9 · FRANZISKA KOZINA, Hüblersdochter · katholisch · weiblich · ALTER 11 Jahre · MASERN · A. Graf". Baptised 19 September 1853 and dead on 7 March 1864 is ten years and five months; the clerk’s 11 rounds up by seven, which is the ordinary slack of that column. THE CORRECTION: this archive recorded Johann’s child of 1853 as FRANZ, a son, and then asked whether the girl dying of measles in that house was a second child or the same one misread. She is the same one. There is no Franz. The index (sig. 04632, entry 213) writes the given name short and it can be read either way; the register writes FRANCISCA in full and ticks Mädchen. The death register had her right for eleven years before the baptismal register was asked. Her parents are named here for the first time - the death book named none. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00886 image 131, sig. 00895 image 141, sig. 04632 image 246
Ana Kozina||DAUGHTER of Johann Kozina and Ursula Sedej - named by this archive, never dated|baptism|25 July 1856|Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje) 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1832-1870 book p.144 - "Juli 25. · 25. · Ober do [Oberfeichting] · 9 · ANNA · katholisch · Mädchen · ehelich · Vater: JOHANN KOZINA, do. [Hüblar] · Mutter: URSULA SEDEJ". BORN AND BAPTISED THE SAME DAY, 25 JULY 1856, at Oberfeichting 9. This archive has carried her as "ANA 1856" since 21 September 2026 - a name taken from the index and never opened. The page was opened on 27 September 2026 while the K section was being counted, and it gives her the day, the house, the sex column and both parents. SHE IS THE MIDDLE OF THREE SISTERS: Franziska 1853, Anna 1856, Maria 1859, born to Johann and Ursula in six years in one cottage. She was seven when Franziska died of measles in that house and twelve when her father died in it. WHAT IS NOT KNOWN is what became of her: she is not in the 1836-1869 death register, which this archive walked in full, so she was alive in 1870. SHE DID NOT MARRY IN THIS PARISH, and that is now a walked negative rather than an absence of looking. On 27 September 2026 both marriage registers that could hold her were read: sig. 03918 (1856-1881) from image 58, which the year cells place at 1874 - the earliest she could marry - to the end of the volume, and sig. 03919 (1881-1899) IN FULL, all seventy-one openings. The groom’s and the bride’s surname columns were cropped from every opening and tiled five to a sheet. THERE ARE THREE KOZINA BRIDES IN THOSE TWENTY-FIVE YEARS and none of them is Anna: her sister MINA in 1883, FRANCIŠKA, daughter of Jožef Kozina, in 1897, and MARIJA, daughter of Urban Kozina, in 1898. So Anna either died unmarried outside the 1836-1869 death register this archive has walked, married in another parish, or left. Her death is not in 1836-1869; the volumes for 1870-1890 and 1890-1911 were read for Gertraud and gave one Kozina woman who is now identified as her sister, so ANNA IS IN NEITHER OF THOSE UNDER THE NAME KOZINA. Nothing further is known. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00886 image 145, sig. 04632 image 246, sig. 03918 images 58-94, sig. 03919 images 1-71
Antonija Česen||DAUGHTER of Kancijan Česen and Marija Kozina - the third of their children to die|death|26 February 1895|Stražišče 84, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Mrliška knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1890-1911 book p.44, entry 23 - "1895, Februar · 26. umrla, 28. pokopana · STRAŽIŠČE · 84 · ANTONIJA ČESEN, hišarja hči · katoliške · ženskega · STAROST 1 1/2 LET · BOŽJAST · ni previdena". BORN ABOUT AUGUST 1893 and dead at eighteen months of the falling sickness, without the sacraments - which for an infant means it was quick. SHE IS NOT NAMED AS ANYBODY’S DAUGHTER IN THIS ENTRY, only "a cottager’s daughter" at house 84. The identification is the house and the surname: Stražišče 84 is where KANCIJAN ČESEN, hišar-dninar, and MARIJA roj. KOZINA lost Kancijan in 1892 and Pavla in 1893, and where Marija herself died on 2 April 1895. SHE DIED FIVE WEEKS BEFORE HER MOTHER, and she was conceived in the year her sister Pavla died. THREE CHILDREN AND THEN THE MOTHER, in one house in three years. Found on 27 September 2026 by re-walking the register for ČESEN after it had been walked for KOZINA and given nothing. Matricula, NSAL sig. 03917 image 45
Maria Kozina of 1859||DAUGHTER of Johann Kozina and Ursula Sedej - a sister the archive did not have|baptism|7 August 1859|Oberfeichting (Zgornje Bitnje) 9, župnija Kranj-Šmartin|Krstna knjiga Kranj-Šmartin 1832-1870 book p.159 - "August 7. · 7. · Oberfeichting · 9 · MARIA · katholisch · Mädchen · ehelich · Vater: JOHANN KOZINA, Hüblar · Mutter: URSULA SEDEJ · Paten Urbas Verčič and Marianna Berčič". BORN AND BAPTISED THE SAME DAY, 7 AUGUST 1859, at Oberfeichting 9 - Johann’s house, the house his father held before him and his nephew Martin was born in. She is Johann’s sixth known child and the third by Ursula Sedej, after Franziska 1853 and Ana 1856. HOW SHE WAS FOUND: not by looking for her. On 27 September 2026 the K section of the baptismal index for 1832-1870 was read end to end to settle a count, and she is entry 262 - "Maria Kozina - 159" - a name the archive had never carried. The count of FIVE Kozina baptisms in that volume was short by her. HER FATHER WAS SIXTY-ONE when she was born on this book’s own arithmetic - he died in 1868 aged 64 - so she was nine when she lost him, and her sister Franziska had died of measles in that house when she was four. WHAT IS NOT KNOWN is what became of her: she is not in the 1836-1869 death register, which this archive walked in full, so she was alive in 1870. AND WHAT BECAME OF HER IS NOW KNOWN, on the same day she was found. She married KANCIJAN ČESEN, a cottager’s son of STRAŽIŠČE 120, in the summer of 1883, aged 23 - and the marriage entry gives her residence as the RAILWAY STATION AT PODNART and her birthplace as "rojena v Zgornjem Bitnju št. 9", with her parents as JANEZ KOZINA, gruntar, and URŠA SEDEJ. SHE IS THEREFORE THE SAME WOMAN as the "Marija Kozina" this file carried as UNPLACED for six days - the only Kozina woman the archive found in twenty-five years of the 1890-1911 death register, known there only as the mother of two children who died at Stražišče 84 in 1892 and 1893. The two rows are one person and both now say so. Matricula, NSAL sig. 00886 image 160, sig. 04632 image 247, sig. 03919 image 15
Leonard John Zubrinich||infant son of Michael Valentine Zubrinić and Minnie Doris, not in the tree|death|23 May 1919|Pirie West, South Australia|The Recorder (Port Pirie) 24 May 1919, Family Notices - "ZUBRINICH. On the 23rd of May at the residence of his grandparents, 10th street, Pirie West, LEONARD JOHN, dearly loved infant son of M. and M. V. ZUBRINICH, AGED 5 WEEKS." So born about mid-April 1919. MICHAEL VALENTINE ZUBRINIĆ (1899-1985) is in this tree with no spouse and no children recorded; this infant and his mother are neither. Found by walking Trove's Family Notices category for Zubrinich in South Australia, 27-28 September 2026. Trove nla.news-article95415266
Minnie Doris||wife of Michael Valentine Zubrinić - not in the tree|marriage and death|by 1919; died 9 December 1932|Solomontown, South Australia|The Recorder (Port Pirie) 12 December 1932, Family Notices - "ZUBRINICH. At Solomontown, on December 9, MINNIE DORIS, dearly beloved WIFE OF MICHAEL V. ZUBRINICH, aged 35 years. At Rest." Born about 1897. She and Michael had already lost an infant son, Leonard John, in 1919 - thirteen years before her own death at thirty-five. No maiden name given in this notice; not yet searched for. Trove nla.news-article96018781
Irene Dorothy Patten||wife of John Stephen Zubrinich - not in the tree|marriage|26 May 1928|Whyalla Methodist Church, South Australia|The Recorder (Port Pirie) 7 June 1928, Family Notices, Wedding - "ZUBRINICH – PATTEN. On May 26, in the Whyalla Methodist Church, by the Rev Howlings, JOHN STEPHEN, eldest son of Mr. and Mrs J. Zubrinich, of Solomontown, to IRENE DOROTHY, eldest daughter of Mr and Mrs F. Patten, Whyalla." JOHN STEPHEN ZUBRINICH (1907-1999) is in this tree with no spouse recorded. Her father is "Mr F. Patten" of Whyalla; not otherwise identified. Trove nla.news-article95785107
Asta Louise Hudson||wife of Leonard Francis Zubrinich - not in the tree|marriage|23 May 1936|Holy Trinity, North Terrace, Adelaide|The Chronicle (Adelaide) 21 May 1936, Family Notices - "HUDSON – ZUBRINICH. The marriage of ASTA LOUISE, only daughter of Mr. and Mrs. S. Hudson, of Bowden, to LEONARD FRANCIS, second son of Mr. and Mrs. J. Zubrinich, of Port Pirie, will be solemnised at Holy Trinity, North terrace, on May 23rd." LEONARD FRANCIS ZUBRINICH (1908-1981) is in this tree with no spouse recorded. The engagement was announced 31 December 1932 (The Advertiser); the marriage itself was more than three years later. Their son DARYL FRANCIS was born 10 June 1939 at Glenelg Private Hospital - The Advertiser 12 June 1939 names the mother "nee Asta Hudson", confirming the marriage held. Trove nla.news-article92339824, nla.news-article35189088, nla.news-article49811426
Eva Uhe||wife of Leonard James Zubrinich - not in the tree|marriage|by 1922|Broken Hill, New South Wales|Barrier Miner (Broken Hill) Family Notices, 14 June 1922 and repeatedly to 1954 - "the FRIENDS of Mr. and Mrs. L. ZUBRINICH are respectfully informed that the Funeral of their late beloved BROTHER and BROTHER-IN-LAW (Roy Leslie)" - her brother's death names her married surname. LEONARD JAMES ZUBRINICH (1894-1985) is in this tree, born Port Pirie, died Broken Hill, with no spouse recorded. Her mother FRANCES EVELINE UHE died 12 February 1944 at 724 Lane Street, Broken Hill, the same address the family gives throughout the 1940s. Three daughters found with her: Elaine May, Shirley and Irene Dawn "Dawn" Zubrinich. In Memoriam notices confirm the given name "Eva" from 1952 onward - "sadly missed by his mother and father-in-law, Eva and Len Zubrinich". Trove nla.news-article45575571, nla.news-article143781484
Elaine May Zubrinich||daughter of Leonard James Zubrinich and Eva Uhe - not in the tree|marriage|engaged Christmas 1942, married by September 1943|Broken Hill, New South Wales|Barrier Miner (Broken Hill) 5 January 1942, Family Notices - "ZUBRINICH — PAYNTER. On Christmas Day, the engagement was announced of ELAINE MAY, eldest daughter of Mr. and Mrs. L. Zubrinich, of 178 Murton Street, to Corporal ALFRED VERDUN (of Darwin), only son of Mr. and Mrs. Joseph Paynter, of 36 Cobalt Street". Married as "May" by the Approaching Marriages notice of 22 September 1943, Oxide Street Methodist Church. Her husband, CORPORAL ALFRED VERDUN PAYNTER, died before October 1951, when his own In Memoriam names Eva and Len Zubrinich as mourning parents-in-law. Trove nla.news-article48395600, nla.news-article143777086
Shirley Zubrinich, married Reed||daughter of Leonard James Zubrinich and Eva Uhe - not in the tree|marriage|engaged 1943, married 15 June 1946|Oxide Street Methodist Church, Broken Hill, New South Wales|Barrier Miner (Broken Hill) 8 June 1946, Family Notices - "ZUBRINICH-REED. The marriage of SHIRLEY, second daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Lin Zubrinich, of 178 Murton Street, to JOHN, eldest son of the late Mr. and Mrs. Cec. Reed, of Broken Hill, will be solemnised in the Oxide Street Methodist Church on Saturday, June 15". "Lin" is a third spelling of Leonard James's own name, beside "L.", "L.J." and "Len" across the same notices. Trove nla.news-article49541140, nla.news-article48471526
Irene Dawn Zubrinich, married McAvaney||daughter of Leonard James Zubrinich and Eva Uhe - not in the tree|marriage|engaged 26 April 1947, married by March 1948|Sacred Heart Cathedral, Broken Hill, New South Wales|Barrier Miner (Broken Hill) 26 April 1947, Family Notices - "ZUBRINICH — McAVANEY. The engagement is announced of IRENE DAWN, youngest daughter of Mr. and Mrs. L. J. Zubrinich, of 178 Murton Street, to EDWARD JOHN (Jack), only son of Mr. and Mrs. Herb McAvaney". The marriage notice of 10 March 1948 gives the venue. A son, JOHN REX McAVANEY, was born 21 July 1949 at the B.H. and District Hospital - "Mrs. McAvaney was formerly Miss Dawn Zubrinich" - confirming the marriage held. Trove nla.news-article48495417, nla.news-article141690592, nla.news-article48609250
Niko Kalanj||son of Juro Kalanj and Ana, of Brinje house 231 - not in the tree|marriage|16 [month illegible] 1890|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 530, entry no. 13 - "KALANJ NIKO", bachelor, 40, of Brinje house 231, son of KALANJ JURO and ANA, married a widow recorded as MARIJA (surname read as "Vučić" or similar, not certain), 33, of Brinje house 198. Witnesses Zoričić Stjepan and Rimenović Tomo; officiated by the parish priest, signed "Šrobi Šimun". NOT IN THE TREE, AND NOT THE SAME GENERATION AS ANYONE PUBLISHED: the tree's Klenovica Kalanji begin on the coast with Petrus Kalanj and Magdalena Butković at house 22, born from the 1830s on. Niko, born about 1850, and his father JURO KALANJ, born perhaps the 1810s-1820s, are the first Kalanj men this archive has found actually resident at Brinje itself, independent of the bare parish name in the 1864 Klenovica baptism that first sent this archive looking. Whether Juro's family is an earlier generation of the same Klenovica line, or a separate Brinje branch, is not established.
Vid Borić||son of Luka Borić, of Kamenica (a hamlet of Brinje parish) - not in the tree|marriage|27 [month illegible] 1890|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 530, entry no. 13 (facing page) - "BORIĆ ___", recorded here as "Vid" though the given name is genuinely hard to read and this is a best guess, not a confident transcription; widower(?), 25, of Kamenica house 17, son of BORIĆ LUKA, married a woman recorded as (Š)orić Kate, 20, of Brinje house 127. A second witness on the same entry is BORIĆ JOZO. NOT IN THE TREE: this archive's /kalanj/ page already names a Jure Borić of Brinje, from the 1910 Stipe Kalanj emigration papers, whose daughter Ana Borić married into the Papić family - this entry is the first independent confirmation from the parish register itself that Borić is a real, resident surname at Kamenica, with at least three men attested in 1890 (Luka, this groom, and Jozo). Whether any of them is kin to the Jure Borić already named on this archive's own page is not established.
Juko Borić||son of Ivan Borić, of Brinje house 126 - not in the tree|marriage|7 July 1890|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 533, entry no. 19 - "BORIĆ JUKO" (the given name could also be read "Jako"), widower, 38, of Brinje house 126, son of BORIĆ IVAN, married Zorčić Matija, spinster, 29, of Brinje house 85, daughter of Zorčić Ivan. Witnesses Javor Niko and a second name not confidently read. NOT IN THE TREE. The second Borić household this archive has found in one pass of one register image-range (493-539): this one at Brinje itself rather than the Kamenica hamlet where Vid Borić's family is recorded. Whether Ivan Borić's household and Luka Borić's household (see Vid Borić, this file) are related is not established.
Miko Borić||widower, of Križ Kamenica - not in the tree|marriage|circa 1890|Križ Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 535 - "BORIĆ MIKO", widower, 55, of "Križ Kamenica" house 33, married Ane Petrak, widow, 41, of Brinje house 143. The entry number and exact date were cut off at the edge of the frame and want a second look. NOT IN THE TREE. A third Borić household, and the second at Kamenica (after Luka and Vid Borić, this file) — Miko's own generation, born about 1835, is the earliest-born Borić this archive has yet put a year to.
Niko Borić||of Brinje house 142 - not in the tree|marriage|24 [month illegible] 1890|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 538, entry no. 28 - "BORIĆ NIKO", bachelor, 25, of Brinje house 142, married a woman recorded as Bašić Marija (surname uncertain), spinster, 22, of Brinje house 105. A witness on the same entry may also be a Borić, not confidently read. NOT IN THE TREE. A fourth Borić man found across images 530-538 of this one register, alongside Luka, Vid, Ivan, Juko and Miko (this file) — Borić is not a marginal surname at Brinje parish, it is one of the more frequent grooms' surnames in these forty-odd images alone.
Marija Borić||daughter of Niko Borić, of Brinje house 142 - not in the tree|marriage|circa 1892-1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 564, entry no. 13 - "BORIĆ MARIJA", spinster, 19, of Brinje house 142, daughter of BORIĆ NIKO, married Hofjenc Niko, bachelor, 28, of Brinje house 154, son of Hofjenc Petar and Marija. NOT IN THE TREE. A PUZZLE, STATED RATHER THAN SMOOTHED OVER: her father is named Niko Borić of Brinje house 142 - the same name and house number as the bachelor Niko Borić who married in 1890 (see Niko Borić, this file, image 538). A 19-year-old daughter marrying in 1892-93 implies a father born by the early 1870s at the latest, which sits awkwardly against a father recorded as a first-time bachelor groom in 1890. Either two Niko Borić men shared house 142 a generation apart, or one of the two entries' ages or marital status was misread, or misattributed here. Not resolved, and not guessed at further.
Mijo Kalanj||of Brinje house 249 - not in the tree|marriage|15 [month illegible] 1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 566 - "KALANJ MIJO", bachelor, 55, of Brinje house 249, married Krnarić Manoš (Manda?), spinster, 23, of Brinje house 168, daughter of Krnarić Jure. A witness on the same entry is KALANJ MATE. NOT IN THE TREE. A second Brinje address for the surname: Niko and Juro Kalanj (this file) are of house 231; Mijo, born about 1838 and the oldest-born Kalanj this archive has a year for, is of house 249, with a further Kalanj - Mate - standing witness. Three named Kalanj men now, across two houses, independent of the coastal Klenovica line the tree already holds. Whether either Brinje household connects to Josephus Kalanj, whose 1864 baptism first sent this archive to the parish, remains unestablished.
Đuso Perković||daughter of Jozo Perković, of Brinje house 145 - not in the tree|marriage|circa 1893-1894|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 581 - "PERKOVIĆ ĐUSO" (the given name is abbreviated and hard to expand with confidence; possibly Đurđa), widow, 23, of Brinje house 145, daughter of PERKOVIĆ JOZO, married Vuković Marko, bachelor, 25, of Brinje house 105. NOT IN THE TREE. The first Perković found here as a named PARTY rather than a witness — two earlier sightings in this book (images 496 and 574) were both witnesses named Perković Mate and Perković Joso. Her father, Jozo Perković, may or may not be one of those two witnesses; not established. This is the surname the Gospić letter specifically asked this archive to find at Brinje, and it is now attested as a real, resident family rather than only a name in a letter.
Ive Borić||son of Jozo Borić, of Križ Kamenica - not in the tree|marriage|23 July 1893|Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 586, entry no. 21 - "BORIĆ IVE", bachelor, 25, of Križ Kamenica, son of BORIĆ JOZO, married Sertić Ane, spinster, 24, of Brinje-Kamenica. A second witness on the same entry is BORIĆ TOMO. NOT IN THE TREE. A sixth and seventh named Borić man (Ive the groom, Tomo the witness), and a second Jozo Borić — whether the same Jozo who witnessed Niko Kalanj's marriage in 1890 (see Niko Kalanj, this file) or a different man of the same name is not established. Borić now has named men at four locations: Brinje itself, Kamenica, Križ Kamenica, and as witnesses across several unrelated entries.
Luce Borić||daughter of Ivan/Ive Borić, of Brinje house 126 - not in the tree|marriage|21 January 1894|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 595, entry no. 3 - "BORIĆ LUCE", widow, 27, of Brinje house 126, daughter of BORIĆ IVE and Mare, married Sertić Tove, bachelor, 28, of Brinje house 288. A witness on the same entry is BORIĆ JURO. NOT IN THE TREE. LIKELY SIBLING OF JUKO BORIĆ, STATED AS A LIKELIHOOD AND NOT ASSERTED: Juko Borić (this file, image 533) is recorded as son of "Borić Ivan" at the same Brinje house 126, marrying in 1890. "Ive" is the ordinary short form of "Ivan," and a shared house number this exact is not a coincidence this archive has seen elsewhere without it meaning something — but the two records do not name each other, and no baptism ties them together, so this stays a strong likelihood rather than a fact. NOT the same "Ive Borić" who married at Kamenica in July 1893 as son of Jozo Borić (this file, image 586) — that man cannot be a 27-year-old woman's father six months after his own first marriage; two different men named Ive Borić are now on record.
Marko Perković||son of Pere Perković, of Novi Kut (Brinje parish) - not in the tree|marriage|25 August 1895|Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 625 - "PERKOVIĆ MARKO", widower, of "N. Kut" (read as Novi Kut, a Brinje-area hamlet; not fully certain), son of PERKOVIĆ PERE and Luce, married Dublić Ane, widow, 61, of Plaščica. A witness on the same entry is BORIĆ MATE. NOT IN THE TREE. A third Perković individual (after Đuso and her father Jozo, this file) and a third generation named: Marko's own father Pere Perković. Perković now has attested men or women at three points: Brinje itself (the witnesses at images 496 and 574), Brinje house 145 (Đuso and her father Jozo), and Novi Kut (Marko and his father Pere). Whether these are one extended family or several unrelated Perković households in the same small parish is not established.
Miko Perković||son of Marko Perković, of Novi Kut (Brinje parish) - not in the tree|marriage|8 November 1897|Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 653 - "PERKOVIĆ MIKO", bachelor, 27, of "M. Kut" (the same hamlet read as Novi Kut for Marko Perković, this file), son of PERKOVIĆ MARKO and Luce, married Bublić Ruse, spinster, 26, of Plaščica. NOT IN THE TREE. A THIRD PERKOVIĆ GENERATION, traced entirely from this one register: PERE PERKOVIĆ (grandfather, named as Marko's father at image 625) — MARKO PERKOVIĆ (father, married the widow Dublić Ane in 1895) — MIKO PERKOVIĆ (this entry, 1897). The mother's name given here, Luce, does not match Marko's 1895 bride Ane, which most likely means Marko had an earlier wife named Luce, Miko's mother, before the 1895 marriage this file already records — stated as a likely reading, not confirmed by any document naming both wives together.
Marija Borić||daughter of a second, distinct Niko Borić, of Kamenica - not in the tree|marriage|22 November 1897|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 656, entry no. 35 - "BORIĆ MARIJA", spinster, 19, of Kamenica house 24, daughter of BORIĆ NIKO and Bare, married Sertić Tave, widower, 33, of Kamenica house 13. NOT IN THE TREE. A SECOND WOMAN OF THIS EXACT NAME, KEPT SEPARATE FROM THE FIRST ON PURPOSE: this archive already holds a Marija Borić, spinster, 19, daughter of a Niko Borić, married Hofjenc Niko around 1892-93 (this file, image 564) — but that woman was of Brinje house 142 with a mother named Marta, married roughly five years earlier, and cannot be the same 19-year-old marrying here in November 1897 at Kamenica house 24 with a mother named Bare. Two different Niko Borić men, each with a daughter named Marija who married at 19, five years and one hamlet apart — read plainly as coincidence in a parish where both names are common, not forced into one identity.
Mile Borić||of Križ Kamenica, son of a father of the same name - not in the tree|marriage|21 [month illegible] 1898|Križ Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga vjenčanih 1888-1899 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 661, entry no. 9 - "BORIĆ MILE", bachelor, 26, of Križ Kamenica house 12, son of BORIĆ MILE and Stoja, married Mesić Mande, spinster, 18, of Brinje-Kamenica house 12. A witness on the same entry may also be a Perković, not confidently read. NOT IN THE TREE. The father is entered under the identical name, Mile Borić — read as written rather than corrected, since a shared name across a generation is exactly the pattern already seen with Niko Borić and Ive Borić elsewhere in this file. An eighth named Borić man, at a fourth Brinje-area house number.
Juraj Borić||son of Tome Borić and Jela, both of Brinje house 141 - not in the tree|baptism|3 February 1888|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 12, entry no. 11 - "BORIĆ JURAJ", male, born 3 February 1888 and baptised the next day, of Brinje house 141, son of BORIĆ TOME and BORIĆ JELA - the mother's own maiden surname is also entered as Borić, meaning this is a Borić man married to a Borić woman. Godparents Benić Juraj and Mrčić Manda. NOT IN THE TREE. A tenth and eleventh Borić name (Tome the father, Juraj the son) at a fifth Brinje-area house (141), and the first sign that the surname intermarried with itself at Brinje - worth watching for as the rest of this register is read, since a Borić-Borić marriage this early may be the root the later Borić households (Kamenica, Križ Kamenica, Brinje 126 and 142) all come down from.
Ane Kalanj||wife of Grgo Dražičević, of Brinje - not in the tree|birth of a child|13 February 1888|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 13, entry no. 15 - the birth of "DRAŽIČEVIĆ JURAJ", male, of Brinje house 196, names his mother's maiden surname as "KALANJ ANE". NOT IN THE TREE. The first Kalanj WOMAN this archive has found at Brinje, married out of the surname into the Dražičević family - one of the most frequently recorded surnames throughout this register. Not yet linked to Niko, Juro or Mijo Kalanj (this file), the three Kalanj men already found in the marriage volume, but a fourth branch of the surname at Brinje regardless.
Ane Kalanj, wife of Krmarić Viol||wife of Viol Krmarić, of Brinje - not in the tree|birth of a child|28 April 1888|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 18 - the birth of "KRMARIĆ MARIJA", female, names her mother's maiden surname as "KALANJ ANE". NOT IN THE TREE. A SECOND WOMAN NAMED ANE KALANJ, KEPT SEPARATE FROM THE FIRST ON PURPOSE: this archive already holds an Ane Kalanj who married Grgo Dražičević and had a son Juraj on 13 February 1888 (this file, image 13) - only weeks before this birth. Whether this is the same woman recorded with a different husband by clerical error, two sisters both named Ana, or simply two unrelated Kalanj women sharing the parish's most common given name is not established and not guessed at. Both entries are kept as written.
Stjepan Borić||son of Stjepan Borić and a mother of maiden surname Vučetić, of Brinje house 28 - not in the tree|baptism|4 February 1890|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 88, entry no. 16 - "BORIĆ STJEPAN", male, born 4 February 1890, of Brinje house 28, son of BORIĆ STJEPAN and VUČETIĆ [given name read as Ove or Ana, not fully certain]. Witnesses Perkić Mijo and [R]abotić Matija - Perkić, not Perković, a surname this archive has now met twice at Brinje and keeps distinct from it. NOT IN THE TREE. A father and son sharing the name Stjepan Borić, the same generational pattern already seen with Niko Borić and Mile Borić elsewhere in this file, at a Brinje house number (28) not yet recorded for the surname.
Marija Borić, wife of Vičić Jure||mother of Vičić Tomo, of Brinje - not in the tree|birth of a child|10 February 1890|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 89, entry no. 19 - the birth of "VIČIĆ TOMO", male, names his mother's maiden surname as "BORIĆ MARIJA". No house number is entered. NOT IN THE TREE. Another Borić woman married out of the surname, the same pattern already seen with Borić's own intermarriage (Tome Borić x Jela Borić, this file) and with the Kalanj women married into Dražičević and Krmarić - Borić now attested marrying into at least three other Brinje families (Hofjenc, Vičić, and itself).
Ivo Borić||son of Ivan Borić and a mother also of the Borić surname, of Brinje house 191 - not in the tree|baptism|September 1890 [exact day not confidently read]|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 106, entry no. 87 - "BORIĆ IVO", male, of Brinje house 191, son of BORIĆ IVAN and a mother entered under the same surname, BORIĆ. Witnesses Rekić Roko and a second name not confidently read. NOT IN THE TREE. A SECOND Borić-marries-Borić household, distinct from the one already in this file at house 141 (Tome Borić and Jela Borić) - two different Brinje houses where the surname intermarried with itself, which is starting to look less like an isolated event and more like a real feature of how this surname sits in the parish.
Petar Borić||son of Tome Borić and Jela Borić, of Brinje house 141 - a sibling of Juraj Borić, this file - not in the tree|baptism|15 October 1890|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 113, entry no. 115 - "BORIĆ PETAR", male, born 15 October 1890, of Brinje house 141, son of BORIĆ TOME and BORIĆ JELA. A margin note added decades later appears to record a civil-era event (illegible in full). NOT IN THE TREE. A SECOND CHILD of the same Borić-marries-Borić household already in this file (Juraj Borić, image 12, born 3 February 1888) - the same house number, the same two parent names, two and a half years apart. This is now a confirmed sibling pair, not just a repeated household.
Viol Kalanj||of Brinje house 118, married to Zoričić Kate - not in the tree|birth of a child|26 December 1890|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 116, entry no. 138 - the birth of "KALANJ KATE", female, of Brinje house 118, names her father as "KALANJ VIOL" and her mother as "ZORIČIĆ KATE". Witnesses Fumić Jure and Marija. NOT IN THE TREE. A THIRD Kalanj house number at Brinje, distinct from Niko and Juro's house 231 and Mijo and Mate's house 249 (both this file, from the marriage book) - a third resident Kalanj household, independent of the other two.
Ivan Borić, witness at Brinje house 138||witness to the baptism of Radotić Dare, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|31 March 1891|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 122, entry no. 20 - the baptism of "RADOTIĆ DARE", female, of Brinje house 138, daughter of Radotić Niko and Lokmer Luce, names "BORIĆ IVAN" as a witness alongside Sertić Marija. NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only, no house number of his own given - kept separate from the several other Borić men already named Ivan/Ive in this file (Ive Borić of Kamenica, the fathers named Ivan at houses 126 and 191) since nothing here ties him to any of them.
Marija Borić, wife of Frane Jurajić||mother of Jurajić Ivo, of Brinje - not in the tree|birth of a child|10 August 1891|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 137, entry no. 78 - the birth of "JURAJIĆ IVO", male, names his mother's maiden surname as "BORIĆ MARIJA". A witness on the same entry is "BORIĆ GRGO". NOT IN THE TREE. A fourth Borić woman married out of the surname (after the one at house 141 who married a Borić man, and the one who married into Vičić) - and a new Borić given name, Grgo, as witness alongside her.
Viol Borić||son of Niko Borić and Marica Bošnjić, of Brinje house 142 - not in the tree|baptism|2 September 1891|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 140, entry no. 93 - "BORIĆ VIOL", male, born 2 September 1891, of Brinje house 142, son of BORIĆ NIKO and BOŠNJIĆ MARICA. A margin note added decades later appears to record his own later civil marriage (not fully legible). NOT IN THE TREE. This is very likely the first child of the Niko Borić already in this file as a 25-year-old bachelor marrying in 1890 (marriage book, image 538) at the same house number, 142 - the timing fits exactly. It also bears on the open puzzle already logged for that Niko: a Marija Borić married out of house 142 around 1892-93 calling herself his daughter, which the ages never supported. A son born in September 1891 makes that impossibility sharper still - this Niko was raising an infant, not marrying off a grown daughter.
Ove Borić, wife of Ivan Javor||mother of Javor Ruse, of Brinje house 41 - not in the tree|birth of a child|3 September 1891|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 141, entry no. 97 - the birth of "JAVOR RUSE", female, of Brinje house 41, names her mother's maiden surname as "BORIĆ OVE". NOT IN THE TREE. A fifth Borić woman married out of the surname (after the ones married into Hofjenc, Vičić, Jurajić, and the Borić-Borić marriage at house 141) - Borić women marrying out at Brinje is now a repeated, not isolated, pattern.
Manole Borić, wife of Tomo Dražičević||mother of Dražičević Marija, of Kamenica house 24 - not in the tree|birth of a child|9 September 1891|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 143, entry no. 104 - the birth of "DRAŽIČEVIĆ MARIJA", female, of Kamenica house 24, names her mother's maiden surname as "BORIĆ MANOLE". Witnesses Javor Ivan and Draženović Matija. NOT IN THE TREE. A sixth Borić woman married out of the surname - and worth watching rather than asserting: this archive's marriage book already holds a Marija Borić of this same address, Kamenica house 24, daughter of a second, distinct Niko Borić (married out in 1897, this file). Whether Manole is that Niko's sister, his wife under a different name, or simply a second unrelated Borić family sharing the house number is not established.
Luce Borić, of Kamenica||unmarried mother of Marko Borić, of Kamenica - not in the tree|birth of a child|17 October 1891|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 152, entry no. 138 - "BORIĆ MARKO", male, of Kamenica, father's column left blank, son of "BORIĆ LUCE" alone - the child takes his unmarried mother's surname. Witnesses Lovinčić Ivan and Borić Matija. NOT IN THE TREE. A Borić woman recorded without a husband, and a Borić witness (Matija) not yet tied to any household in this file - kept separate from the Luce Borić already here (daughter of Ivan/Ive Borić, Brinje house 126, married 1894) since nothing ties this Kamenica woman to that Brinje one beyond the shared given name and surname.
Marija Borić, wife of Jure Vičić||mother of a second Vičić Tomo, of Brinje house 197 - not in the tree|birth of a child|21 December 1891|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 160, entry no. 170 - the birth of "VIČIĆ TOMO", male, of Brinje house 197, names his parents as "VIČIĆ JURE" and "BORIĆ MARIJA". NOT IN THE TREE. A puzzle worth stating plainly rather than resolving: this file already holds a birth of a "VIČIĆ TOMO" to a father named Vičić Jure and a mother of maiden surname Borić Marija, ten months earlier (10 February 1890, image 89, entry no. 19). Same father's name, same mother's maiden name, same child's name, twenty-two months apart. Read as written: either the same couple naming a second son after an elder Tomo who did not survive infancy - not unusual for this period - or the same event entered twice by the clerk. No document says which, and this row does not guess.
Matija Borić||daughter of Tome Borić, of Brinje house 141 - a third sibling alongside Juraj and Petar Borić, this file - not in the tree|baptism|19 December 1892|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 165, entry no. 18 - "BORIĆ MATIJA", female, of Brinje house 141, daughter of BORIĆ TOME and a mother entered under the surname BORIĆ with the given name read as MATIJA - the same given name as the child's own, a reading not fully certain at this resolution. Witnesses Petak Tome and Mace. NOT IN THE TREE. A THIRD CHILD of the same Borić-marries-Borić household already in this file (Juraj, born 1888; Petar, born 1890) - the same house number and father's name, four and a half years after the first child. Whether the mother's name here is genuinely Matija, or a misreading of the Jela already recorded for this household, is not established.
Ove Borić, wife of Ive Ovčarić||mother of Ovčarić Jore, of Lučane - not in the tree|birth of a child|5 August 1893|Lučane, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 179, entry no. 73 - the birth of "OVČARIĆ JORE", male, of Lučane house 36, names his mother's maiden surname as "BORIĆ OVE". A witness on the same entry is "BORIĆ MARKO". NOT IN THE TREE. A seventh Borić woman married out of the surname, and the first Borić name this file has placed at Lučane - every other Borić household so far has been at Brinje itself, Kamenica, or Križ Kamenica. A new Borić given name, Marko, stands witness, not yet tied to any household.
Kate Borić||daughter of Niko Borić, of Kamenica house 24 - not in the tree|baptism|18 February 1893|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 201, entry no. 9 - "BORIĆ KATE", female, of Kamenica house 24, daughter of BORIĆ NIKO and RADOTIĆ DACE. Witnesses Javor Ivan and Luce. NOT IN THE TREE. This is the same house, 24, and almost certainly the same Niko Borić already in this file as father of Marija Borić, who married out of this house in 1897 - but that entry names his wife as Bare, not Dace Radotić recorded here. Not merged: either a second wife, or the same woman under two different names or a clerical inconsistency. Recorded as written, the question left open.
Tome Borić, witness at Brinje house 101||witness to the baptism of Perlić Ane, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|8 January 1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 201, entry no. 8 - the baptism of "PERLIĆ ANE", female, of Brinje house 101, daughter of Perlić Mijo and Vičić Kate, names "BORIĆ TOME" as a witness alongside Rakonić Roza. NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only, no house number of his own given - not yet tied to any household in this file, and kept separate from the several other men named Tome/Tomo already here.
Stjepan Borić, son of Grgo Borić||son of Grgo Borić, of Brinje house 126 - not in the tree|baptism|20 August 1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 203, entry no. 15 - "BORIĆ STJEPAN", male, of Brinje house 126, son of BORIĆ GRGO and MILAKOVIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses Milaković Grgo and Kate. NOT IN THE TREE. The same house number, 126, already in this file for Ivan/Ive Borić's children Juko (married 1890) and Luce (married 1894) - but the father here is named Grgo, not Ivan. Flagged rather than merged: Grgo could be a brother sharing the house, a second household at the same number, or the same man under a different name; none of this is established.
Tauka Borić, wife of Jure Sertić||mother of Sertić Ivan, of Kamenica - not in the tree|birth of a child|3 April 1893|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 208, entry no. 38 - the birth of "SERTIĆ IVAN", male, of Kamenica, names his mother's maiden surname as "BORIĆ TAUKA" (an unusual given name, read as written, not confidently a diminutive of anything more common). A witness on the same entry is "BORIĆ IVO", alongside Manole. NOT IN THE TREE. An eighth Borić woman married out of the surname. The witness Ivo Borić is kept separate from the Ive Borić already in this file (of Kamenica, son of Jozo Borić, married 1893) since nothing ties the two beyond the shared name and hamlet.
Jozo Borić, witness at Kamenica||witness to the baptism of Sertić Ivan, of Kamenica house 5 - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|24 June 1893|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 215, entry no. 65 - the baptism of "SERTIĆ IVAN", male, of Kamenica house 5, son of Sertić Jure and Dražičević Ova, names "BORIĆ JOZO" as a witness alongside Mesić Toka. NOT IN THE TREE. Kept separate from the Jozo Borić already in this file (father of Ive Borić, of Križ Kamenica, married 1893) - both are Kamenica-area men of the same name at the same date, which makes them a plausible match, but nothing in either document names them as the same person.
Jure Borić, witness at Brinje house 288||witness to the baptism of Sertić Niko, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|25 June 1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 216, entry no. 67 - the baptism of "SERTIĆ NIKO", male, of Brinje house 288, son of Sertić Miho and Pavlak Ove, names "BORIĆ JURE" as a witness alongside Matija. NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only, no house number of his own given - not yet tied to any household in this file.
