Kate Perković, wife of Jure Hofjevac||mother of Hofjevac Luka, of Brinje house 148 - not in the tree|birth of a child|31 August 1896|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 345, entry no. 87 - the birth of "HOFJEVAC LUKA", male, of Brinje house 148, names his parents as "HOFJEVAC JURE" and "PERKOVIĆ KATE". Witnesses Hofjevac Pave i Blažanin Kar[a?]. NOT IN THE TREE. A fourth Perković individual in this file (after Đuso and her father Jozo at house 145, and Marko/Pere/Miko at Novi Kut) and the first Perković woman found - married into the same Hofjenc/Hofjevac family that has already absorbed several Borić women in this file. House 148 is the same number already in this file for Marko Borić, son of Niko Borić and Boletić Marija (image 266) - a coincidence noted, not asserted as meaningful, since the families (Hofjevac and Borić) are otherwise unconnected here.
Kate Borić, wife of Joso Domić||mother of Domić Luce, of Lučane - not in the tree|birth of a child|6 September 1896|Lučane, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 348, entry no. 101 - the birth of "DOMIĆ LUCE", female, of Lučane, names her parents as "DOMIĆ JOSO" and "BORIĆ KATE" - both parents' own birthplace entered as Brinje, though the family now resides at Lučane. Witnesses Bičanić Marko i Domić Kate. NOT IN THE TREE. A fourth person in this file named Kate Borić; nothing ties her to the other three (Kamenica house 24 daughter of Niko, witness at house 85, unmarried mother at Kamenica house 3).
Ivan Bišanić, son of Marko Bišanić and Luce Borić||son of Marko Bišanić and Luce Borić, of Brinje house 174 - a sibling of Franjo Bišanić, this file - not in the tree|baptism|17 September 1896|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 350, entry no. 108 - "BIŠANIĆ IVAN", male, born 17 September 1896, of Brinje house 174, son of BIŠANIĆ MARKO and BORIĆ LUCE - the same house number and both parents' names already in this file for Franjo Bišanić, born August 1894. Witnesses Javor Ivan i Marija. NOT IN THE TREE. A second confirmed child of this household, two years after the first - Luce Borić's marriage into Bišanić is now a real, continuing family, not a single register line.
Niko Sertić, son of Jure Sertić and Tauka Borić||son of Jure Sertić and Tauka Borić, of Kamenica house 13 - a sibling of Ivan Sertić, this file - not in the tree|baptism|1 November 1896|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 356, entry no. 133 - "SERTIĆ NIKO", male, born 1 November 1896, of Kamenica house 13, son of SERTIĆ JURE and BORIĆ TAUKA - the same couple already in this file as parents of Sertić Ivan (born 3 April 1893). NOT IN THE TREE. A second confirmed child of this household, three and a half years after the first - Tauka Borić's marriage into Sertić is now a real, continuing family, not a single register line.
Tome Krnarić, son of Jure Krnarić and Marija Borić||son of Jure Krnarić and Marija Borić, of Brinje house 208 - a sibling of Manda Krnarić, this file - not in the tree|baptism|18 March 1897|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 369, entry no. 23 - "KRNARIĆ TOME", male, born 18 March 1897, of Brinje house 208, son of KRNARIĆ JURE and BORIĆ MARIJA - the same couple already in this file as parents of Krnarić Manda (born 24 May 1894), this time with a house number the earlier entry lacked. Witnesses Vučetić Tome i Jišanić Ave. NOT IN THE TREE. A second confirmed child of this household, three years after the first.
Grgo Borić, witness at Brinje house 74 (1897)||witness to the baptism of Milaković Grgo's child, of Brinje house 74 - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|15 April 1897|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 370, entry no. 27 - the baptism of "MILAKOVIĆ MANOLE", female, of Brinje house 74, daughter of Milaković Grgo and Lasić Kate, names "BORIĆ GRGO" as a witness alongside a woman named Marica. NOT IN THE TREE. A THIRD SIGHTING of this exact pairing: the same Borić Grgo witnessing a Milaković baptism at the very same house 74 where he first appeared in this file (image 239, 1893), and paired with a woman named Marica, the same name paired with him at image 335. Whether all three sightings are the same man, kept separate from the Grgo Borić already in this file as father of Stjepan and Ana Borić at house 126, is not established - but the recurrence of both the house number and the witness's companion's name is the strongest pattern of its kind in this file.
Viol Borić, witness at Brinje (image 381)||witness to a baptism at Brinje, exact child and date not captured in this scan - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|1897|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 381 - only the witness line survives at the very top of this photograph, reading "BORIĆ VIOL i Vukorić Kate" - the entry's own date, house number, child and parents are cut off above the frame the scan captured, evidently the tail end of an entry (probably no. 70) whose main body was not photographed in this item. NOT IN THE TREE. A new Borić given name (Viol, also a Kalanj given name already in this file, though not shared by the same person) - kept on record despite the incomplete citation, since the witness name itself is legible and clear.
Roza Borić, witness at Brinje house 139||witness to the baptism of Raobtić Ive's child, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|September 1897|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 387, entry no. 95 - the baptism of "RAOBTIĆ OVE", female, of Brinje house 139, daughter of Raobtić Ive and Komadina Bare, names "BORIĆ ROZA" as a witness alongside a surname read as Sertić or similar, given name Merko. NOT IN THE TREE. A new Borić given name (Roza), kept separate from all other Borić individuals already in this file since nothing ties her to any of them.
Joso Borić, witness at Brinje house 124||witness to the baptism of Škorup Marko's child, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|3 October 1897|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 390, entry no. 107 - the baptism of "ŠKORUP AVE", female, of Brinje house 124, daughter of Škorup Marko and Vranić Ave, names "BORIĆ JOSO" as a witness alongside Jasović Bare. NOT IN THE TREE. A Škorup-family baptism, the same surname already tied to the plausible Alojz Borić sighting elsewhere in this file (image 338) - kept separate from the two Jozo Borić men already in this file, both placed at Kamenica, since this one is at Brinje itself.
Niko Borić, witness at Brinje house 154||witness to the baptism of Blažanin Niko's child, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|4 December 1897|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, continuing past image 400's "ITEM 2" end card with entry numbers unbroken from the second item), image 406, entry no. 144 - the baptism of "BLAŽANIN TOME", male, of Brinje house 154, son of Blažanin Niko and Violaković Manole, names "BORIĆ NIKO" as a witness alongside Marija. NOT IN THE TREE. Kept separate from the Niko Borić already in this file (married 1890, house 142) and from the two households already in this file fathered by a Niko Borić (house 148; Kamenica house 24), since nothing ties any of them together beyond the shared given name.
Marica Borić, daughter of Niko Borić (house 142)||daughter of Niko Borić and Bojenić Marica, of Brinje house 142 - a probable third child of this household - not in the tree|baptism|23 July 1898|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, continuing past 1897 with entry numbers unbroken), image 427, entry no. 70 - "BORIĆ MARICA", female, born 23 July 1898, of Brinje house 142, daughter of BORIĆ NIKO and BOJENIĆ MARICA. Witnesses (porodično i rodno ime prijavitelja) "BORIĆ TOME" i Hofjevac Marija. NOT IN THE TREE. A PROBABLE THIRD CHILD of the Niko Borić already in this file at house 142 (married 1890 to a wife recorded as Bašić Marija; first child Viol born 1891 to a wife recorded as Bošnjić Marica) - the mother's maiden name is entered a third way here, Bojenić, close enough in sound to Bašić/Bošnjić that all three may be the same woman under three scribal readings, or may not be; not merged, only noted. The witness BORIĆ TOME is kept separate from the Tome Borić already in this file as a lone 1893 witness at house 101 and from the Tome Borić heading his own household at Kamenica house 23, since nothing here ties any of them together.
Borić France, wife of Sertić Jure||mother of Sertić Niko, of Kamenica house 28 - not in the tree|birth of a child|10 October 1898|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries now numbering within calendar year 1898 rather than continuing the running count from item two), image 431, entry no. 86 - "SERTIĆ NIKO", male, born 10 October 1898, of Kamenica house 28, son of SERTIĆ JURE and BORIĆ FRANCE (an unusual given name, read as written). Witnesses "BORIĆ VUJO" and Sertić Ruže. NOT IN THE TREE. A NEW Sertić-Borić couple, kept separate from the Sertić Jure and Tauka Borić already in this file at Kamenica house 13 (parents of Ivan, born 1893, and Niko, born 1896) - a different house number and a different given name for the Borić wife, though the shared given name Jure for both Sertić husbands is left unexplained: possibly the same man with two households, possibly two different men, not established.
Borić Vujo, witness at Kamenica house 28||witness to the baptism of Sertić Niko, of Kamenica - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|10 October 1898|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 431, entry no. 86 - the baptism of "SERTIĆ NIKO", male, of Kamenica house 28, son of Sertić Jure and Borić France, names "BORIĆ VUJO" as a witness alongside Sertić Ruže. NOT IN THE TREE. A new Borić given name (Vujo), kept separate from all other Borić individuals already in this file since nothing ties him to any of them.
Manole Borić, daughter of Alojz Borić||daughter of Alojz Borić and Mesić Manola, of Kamenica house 23 - not in the tree|baptism|3 January 1899|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries now numbering within calendar year 1899), image 449, entry no. 4 - "BORIĆ MANOLE", female, born 3 January 1899, of Kamenica house 23, daughter of BORIĆ ALOJZ and MESIĆ MANOLA. Witnesses (unclear surname) Joso and Femić Marija, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. THIS BEARS DIRECTLY ON TWO PUZZLES ALREADY IN THIS FILE: the same house number, Kamenica 23, already holds Tome Borić (born 1895) son of Borić Tome and Mesić Manda-Marija - a different father's given name but the same house and the same wife's surname, Mesić, for a second time. And ALOJZ BORIĆ himself was already in this file only as a plausible, unconfirmed witness sighting (image 338, circa 1895) tentatively linked to LOJZE BORIĆ of Kamenica house 83 (father of Luce Borić, whose mother was also a Mesić - Manda-Marija). This baptism proves Alojz Borić is a real household head, not merely a witness, but does not by itself resolve whether he is the same man as Tome of house 23, the same man as Lojze of house 83, both, or neither - three Borić men, three readings of a name, two houses, and a wife's surname (Mesić) that keeps recurring, none of it merged here.
Ruže Kalanj, daughter of Jure Kalanj (house 231)||daughter of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Manole, of Brinje house 231 - not in the tree|baptism|5 January 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 450, entry no. 5 - "KALANJ RUŽE", female, born 5 January and registered 8 January 1899, of Brinje house 231, daughter of KALANJ JURE and VUČETIĆ MANOLE. Witnesses Rumenović Jure i Ruce, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. CORRECTED ON RE-READING AT FULL ZOOM, 5 October 2026: the mother's surname was first read as Vukelić and is in fact VUČETIĆ - the same surname as Marija Vučetić, wife of the Niko Kalanj already on record at this same house 231. NOT MERGED, but the link is now a real one: a Kalanj father named Jure (a variant of Juro, the name of Niko's own father) and a Vučetić mother at the very house where Niko Kalanj and Marija Vučetić raised Anica (1893) and Niko (1896). Whether Jure is the same man as Niko under a different given name, a brother who married a Vučetić woman too, or the same Marija Vučetić under a variant given name (Manole) is not established. See also Franc Kalanj, born 28 January 1899 at the same house (this file), whose parents are entered as Kalanj Mile and Vučetić Marija - two Kalanj births at house 231 within four weeks cannot be one child. SURNAME QUESTION SETTLED 5 OCTOBER 2026: the 'Kalauj' near-miss this register's earlier reading kept separate is the same word as Kalanj; the 1891 entry for Marija/Marisa (image 157, this file) names these same parents, Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Manole, at this same house 231. This row is Kalanj without caveat.
Luce Borić, daughter of Tome Borić (house 141)||daughter of Tome Borić and Jela Borić, of Brinje house 141 - a fifth child of that household - not in the tree|baptism|19 January 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 450, entry no. 8 - "BORIĆ LUCE", female, born 19 January 1899 and registered 30 January, of Brinje house 141, daughter of BORIĆ TOME and BORIĆ JELA. Witnesses "BORIĆ NIKO" and Radotić Luce, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. A FIFTH CHILD of the Borić-marries-Borić household at house 141 already in this file (Juraj, 1888; Petar, 1890; Matija, 1892; Ove, 1894) - the same house number and both parents' names, eleven years after the first child. Separate from the Marica daughter of Ive Borić and Matija Borić entered at this same house in 1895, whose parents' names differ. Kept apart from the several other women named Luce Borić already in this file (Kamenica house 24, Kamenica house 83, wife of Marko Bišanić, the widow of house 126) since nothing ties them together beyond the name. The witness Borić Niko is not tied to any of the Niko Borić men already here (houses 142, 148, Kamenica 24, witness at house 154).
Franc Kalanj, son of Mile Kalanj and Vučetić Marija||son of Mile Kalanj and Vučetić Marija, of Brinje house 231 - not in the tree|baptism|28 January 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 451, entry no. 11 - "KALANJ FRANC", male, born 28 January 1899 and registered 29 January, of Brinje house 231, son of KALANJ MILE and VUČETIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses Buhlić Franc i Marija, matičar Vučetić Stipe. NOT IN THE TREE. THE SAME HOUSE AND THE SAME MOTHER'S NAME AS THE NIKO KALANJ HOUSEHOLD ALREADY ON RECORD: Niko Kalanj married in 1890 a widow Marija and lived at Brinje house 231; their children Anica (1893) and Niko (1896) name the mother as Marija Vučetić. This birth names the same house and the same woman's name, but the father's given name reads Mile (clear M, no Niko-like stroke) where Niko would be expected, and a Kalanj Jure with a Vučetić Manole had a daughter at this house three weeks earlier (this file). Kept as a separate entry rather than folded into Niko's household; most likely a continuation of that family, possibly with the father's name misentered or a second Kalanj brother sharing the house and marrying into the same Vučetić family, but neither is established.
Mijo Krnarić, son of Jure Krnarić and Marija Borić||son of Jure Krnarić and Borić Marija, of Brinje house 208 - a third child of that household - not in the tree|baptism|20 March 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 454, entry no. 23 - "KRNARIĆ MIJO", male, born and registered 20 March 1899, of Brinje house 208, son of KRNARIĆ JURE and BORIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses entered as "Perkić Mijo" (the recurring near-miss surname, distinct from Perković) and a second name read as Petrović Manda, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. A THIRD CHILD of the Krnarić-Borić household already in this file (Manda, born 24 May 1894, and Tome, born 18 March 1897) - the same two parents' names, and the same house number, 208, as the 1897 birth. This also steadies the second Krnarić household entered at house 208 in November 1898 (Franjo Krnarić and Javor Marija, image 445 - not in this file as it names no Borić), which now looks like a second family sharing the house rather than a rival reading of this one.
Marija Kalanj, daughter of Viol Kalanj||daughter of Viol Kalanj and Zoričić Kate, of Brinje house 188 - a third child of that household - not in the tree|baptism|13 March 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 454, entry no. 24 - "KALANJ MARIJA", female, born 13 March 1899 and registered 16 March, of Brinje house 188, daughter of KALANJ VIOL and ZORIČIĆ KATE. Witnesses Draženović Joso i Manok, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. A THIRD CHILD of the Viol Kalanj and Kate Zoričić household already in this file (Kate, December 1890, house 118; Franjo, August 1893, house 189) - the same two parents' names, eight years after the second. The house number is a third variant, 188, beside 118 and 189: all three are read as written, and a house number that drifts by one digit across three births to the same parents is probably a scribal habit in the register rather than three addresses. Kept separate from the several women named Marija Kalanj in the tree.
Bare Hofjevac, daughter of Hofjevac Viol and Marija Borić||daughter of Hofjevac Viol (earlier read Vid) and Borić Marija, of Brinje house 160 - a second child of that household - not in the tree|baptism|9 August 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 461, entry no. 51 - "HOFJEVAC BARE", female, born 9 August and registered 10 August 1899, of Brinje house 160, daughter of HOFJEVAC VIOL and BORIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses Hofjevac Marko i Bare, matičar Vučetić Stipe; later marginal notes in a twentieth-century hand. NOT IN THE TREE. A SECOND CHILD of the household already in this file as Marija Borić, wife of Vid Hofjevac (Hofjevac Tome, born 3 January 1895, house 160): the same house number and the same mother. The father's given name is entered here as Viol where the 1895 entry was read as Vid - the two short forms are close enough in this hand that one man under two readings is the natural explanation, not asserted. This is the same eighth Marija Borić already in this file, not a new woman.
Kate Borić, wife of Petar Sertić||mother of Sertić Tomo, of Brinje house 128 - not in the tree|birth of a child|7 August 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 461, entry no. 52 - "SERTIĆ TOMO", male, born 7 August and registered 13 August 1899, of Brinje house 128, son of SERTIĆ PETAR and BORIĆ KATE. Witnesses Jelačić Tomo i BORIĆ JELA, matičar Vučetić Stipe. NOT IN THE TREE. A fifth woman named Kate Borić in this file, kept apart from the Kate Borić who was a witness at house 85, the unmarried mother at Kamenica, the wife of Joso Domić at Lučane and the Kate of Kamenica house 24, since nothing ties any of them together beyond the name. Sertić is the surname Borić women are found marrying into most often in this file: Luce Borić (widow, married Sertić Tove, Brinje 288, 1894), Tauka (Kamenica 13), Marija (married Sertić Tave, Kamenica 13, 1897), France (Kamenica 28) and now Kate (Brinje 128).
Jela Borić, witness at Brinje house 128||witness to the baptism of Sertić Tomo, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|13 August 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 461, entry no. 52 - the baptism of "SERTIĆ TOMO", male, of Brinje house 128, son of Sertić Petar and Borić Kate, names "BORIĆ JELA" as a witness alongside Jelačić Tomo. NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only. The only Borić woman called Jela already in this file is the mother of the house-141 Borić-marries-Borić household (Tome Borić and Jela Borić); this may be her standing up for a Borić relative's child, but nothing in the entry says so and she is not merged with her.
Joso Borić, son of Stipe Borić and Luce Sertić||son of Borić Stipe and Sertić Luce, of Kamenica house 23 - a third Borić household at that house number - not in the tree|baptism|18 August 1899|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 462, entry no. 55 - "BORIĆ JOSO", male, born 18 August and registered 20 August 1899, of Kamenica house 23, son of BORIĆ STIPE and SERTIĆ LUCE (both entered as of Kamenica). Witnesses Blažanin Šime i Marija. Later marginal notes dated 1924 and 1982 record his own later civil events (not fully read). NOT IN THE TREE. KAMENICA HOUSE 23 NOW HOLDS THREE BORIĆ FATHERS IN THIS FILE: Tome Borić (son Tome, 1895, wife Mesić Manda-Marija), Alojz Borić (daughter Manole, January 1899, wife Mesić Manola) and now Stipe Borić (this child, wife Sertić Luce). The wives differ (Mesić, Mesić, Sertić), so these read as three households sharing one house number - the same shape already seen at Kamenica house 24 - rather than one man under three names; but Stipe and the Borić Stjepan who witnessed a Sertić baptism at Kamenica house 5 in 1895 (this file) may be one man, which is a plausible, unconfirmed link and not a merge. Another Borić man marrying a Sertić woman: Sertić is again the partner surname.
Kate Borić, wife of Marko Sertić||mother of Sertić Ruže, of Brinje house 127 - not in the tree|birth of a child|13 August 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 462, entry no. 53 - "SERTIĆ RUŽE", female, born 13 August and registered 15 August 1899, of Brinje house 127, daughter of SERTIĆ MARKO and BORIĆ KATE. Witnesses Jurašić Jure i Mesić Ovca, matičar Vučetić Stipe. NOT IN THE TREE. A SIXTH KATE BORIĆ, AND A PUZZLE STATED RATHER THAN SMOOTHED: the baptism immediately before this one in the register (entry 52, born 7 August, Brinje house 128, this file) names a mother Borić Kate married to Sertić PETAR; this one, six days later at house 127, names a mother Borić Kate married to Sertić MARKO. Two different husbands, two neighbouring house numbers, one mother's name and surname, within a week - two different women both called Kate Borić who married into Sertić, or one woman and a scribal slip on the husband's name or the house. Not resolved, and not guessed at; the two rows are kept separate.
Lojze Borić, witness at Kamenica house 5||witness to the baptism of Sertić Marko, of Kamenica house 5 - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|18 August 1899|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 462, entry no. 54 - the baptism of "SERTIĆ MARKO", male, born and registered 18 August 1899, of Kamenica house 5, son of Sertić Pave and Vučetić Marica, names "BORIĆ LOJZE" as a witness alongside a woman read as Anica (surname not given). NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only. "Lojze" is the short form of Alojz and is the name of the father of Luce Borić at Kamenica house 83 (this file, 1894); the same hamlet, a Sertić baptism, and a name already tied to Alojz Borić of Kamenica house 23 (this file, January 1899) make this a plausible, unconfirmed sighting of that same man - not merged. Kamenica house 5 is also the house where Borić Stjepan witnessed a Sertić baptism in 1895 (this file).
Tome Borić, son of Tome Borić and Radotić Marija (Kamenica house 24)||son of Tome Borić and Radotić Marija, of Kamenica house 24 - a later child of that household - not in the tree|baptism|13 September 1899|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 468, entry no. 79 - "BORIĆ TOME", male, born 13 and registered 14 September 1899, of Kamenica house 24, son of BORIĆ TOME and RADOTIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses Radotić Niko i Rajković Kate, matičar Sertić Šimun; a later marginal note of the 1960s. NOT IN THE TREE. THIS SETTLES A LITTLE OF THE KAMENICA HOUSE-24 PUZZLE: the file already holds Luce Borić, born October 1893 at house 24, daughter of Borić Tome and Radotić Marija - a father named Tome and a mother named Radotić Marija, not the Niko Borić and Bare or Dace named for the other children at that house. This child, six years later, has the same father's name, the same mother's name and the same house, so a Tome Borić x Radotić Marija household at house 24 is now two children deep and reads as a real, separate household beside the Niko Borić one, not a scribal slip for it. Kept apart from the Tome Borić of Kamenica house 23 (wife Mesić Manda-Marija) and from the Tome Borić of Brinje house 141 (wife Jela Borić) - three Borić men called Tome, each with his own wife.
Niko Kalanj, witness at Plašćica 4||witness to the baptism of Buhlić Ivan, of Plašćica - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|28 September 1899|Plašćica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 472, entry no. 94 - the baptism of "BUHLIĆ IVAN", male, born 28 September and registered 1 October 1899, of Plašćica 4, son of Buhlić Franjo and Murat Marija, names "KALANJ NIKO" as a witness alongside Murat Ruže. NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only. The surname reads Kalanj; the Kalauj/Kalanj doubt that this row once carried was settled on 5 October 2026 (see Marija Kalanj, daughter of Jure Kalanj, 1891, this file): Kalauj is Kalanj. The given name Niko is the name of Niko Kalanj of Brinje house 231 (married 1890, this file), who may be standing witness at a neighbouring hamlet's baptism; that is a plausible, unconfirmed link, not a merge.
Ive Hofjevac, son of Niko Hofjevac and Marija Borić (house 154)||son of Hofjevac Niko and Borić Marija, of Brinje house 154 - a later child of that household - not in the tree|baptism|12 November 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 474, entry no. 104 - "HOFJEVAC IVE", male, born 12 and registered 15 November 1899, of Brinje house 154, son of HOFJEVAC NIKO and BORIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses Jelačić Niko i BORIĆ MILKA, matičar Vučetić Stipe. NOT IN THE TREE. A LATER CHILD of the household already in this file: the 1892-93 marriage of Marija Borić (daughter of Niko Borić of house 142) to Hofjenc Niko of Brinje house 154, and their son Niko, born 11 October 1893 (this file) - the same father's name, the same mother's maiden surname and name, and the same house number, 154, as the marriage groom's. Six years after the first child; the spelling is Hofjevac here, as at house 160, but the husband's given name and the house number tie this to the house-154 couple and not to the Vid/Viol Hofjevac of house 160 (Marija Borić number eight), whose own second child was born in August of the same year.
Milka Borić, witness at Brinje house 154||witness to the baptism of Hofjevac Ive, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|15 November 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 474, entry no. 104 - the baptism of "HOFJEVAC IVE", male, of Brinje house 154, son of Hofjevac Niko and Borić Marija, names "BORIĆ MILKA" (given name read as Milka, not fully certain) as a witness alongside Jelačić Niko. NOT IN THE TREE. A new Borić given name, a witness only, plausibly a relative of the child's mother Marija Borić standing up for her child, though the entry does not say so; not tied to any Borić household in this file.
Marija Borić, wife of Stipo Mesić||mother of Mesić Petar, of Kamenica house 20 - not in the tree|birth of a child|14 November 1899|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 475, entry no. 105 - "MESIĆ PETAR", male, born and registered 14 November 1899, of Kamenica house 20, son of MESIĆ STIPO and BORIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses read as Perkić Mijo (the recurring near-miss surname, distinct from Perković) i BORIĆ MARIJA, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. A tenth woman in this file named Marija Borić, and a Borić woman married out of the surname into Mesić - a surname that already appears as the maiden name of the wives of Lojze, Tome and Alojz Borić at Kamenica, so Borić and Mesić are now married to each other in both directions at Kamenica. Kept apart from all nine other Marija Borić women already in this file since nothing ties them together beyond the name.
Marija Borić, witness at Kamenica house 20||witness to the baptism of Mesić Petar, of Kamenica - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|14 November 1899|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 475, entry no. 105 - the baptism of "MESIĆ PETAR", male, of Kamenica house 20, son of Mesić Stipo and Borić Marija, names "BORIĆ MARIJA" as a witness alongside a man read as Perkić Mijo. NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only. She stands up for a child whose own mother is also named Borić Marija (this file): a relative of the mother is the natural reading, possibly even the same name given to two kinswomen, but the entry does not say so and the two women are not merged.
Luce Borić, wife of Pave Sertić||mother of Sertić Manole, of Brinje house 289 - not in the tree|birth of a child|29 October 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 478, entry no. 120 - "SERTIĆ MANOLE", female, born 29 October and registered 1 November 1899, of Brinje house 289, daughter of SERTIĆ PAVE and BORIĆ LUCE. Witnesses Hofjevac Niko i BORIĆ MILKA, matičar Vučetić Stipe. NOT IN THE TREE. A sixth woman named Luce Borić in this file, and the sixth Borić woman found married into Sertić (after Luce at Brinje 288 in 1894, Tauka, Marija, France and the two Kates of August 1899). The widow Luce Borić of house 126 married Sertić Tove at Brinje house 288 in 1894 (this file) - a house next door to this one, 289, and a Sertić husband, though the husband's given name here is Pave, not Tove; whether this is her under a different reading of the husband's name, a younger Luce, or another woman is not established and not guessed at. Kept separate from all five other Luce Borić women in this file.
Milka Borić, witness at Brinje house 289||witness to the baptism of Sertić Manole, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|1 November 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 478, entry no. 120 - the baptism of "SERTIĆ MANOLE", female, of Brinje house 289, daughter of Sertić Pave and Borić Luce, names "BORIĆ MILKA" as a witness alongside Hofjevac Niko. NOT IN THE TREE. THE SAME NAME TWO WEEKS BEFORE ANOTHER SIGHTING: on 15 November 1899 a Borić Milka stood witness at Brinje house 154 beside Jelačić Niko at the baptism of Hofjevac Ive, son of Hofjevac Niko and Marija Borić (this file); here, on 1 November, she stands beside Hofjevac Niko himself. The two sightings are close enough in time, and share Hofjevac Niko closely enough, to read as one woman - probably a kinswoman of Marija Borić, Niko Hofjevac's wife - but the register does not say so and the two rows are not merged.
Manole Kalanj, daughter of Jerko Kalanj and Krnarić Ruže||daughter of Kalanj Jerko (given name read Jerok) and Krnarić Ruže, of Brinje house 188 - a second Kalanj household at that house number - not in the tree|baptism|11 November 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 481, entry no. 131 - "KALANJ MANOLE", female, born 11 and registered 13 November 1899, of Brinje house 188, daughter of KALANJ JEROK (Jerko) and KRNARIĆ RUŽE. Witnesses Bišanić Jerok i Dubčić Manda (surname read with some doubt), matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. A NEW KALANJ FATHER: Jerko, not Viol, Niko, Jure, Mile, Mijo or Mate, as the Kalanj men in this file are named. House 188 is where this file already places Marija Kalanj, born 13 March 1899 to Kalanj Viol and Zoričić Kate (this file) - a different father and a different mother, eight months apart, at the same house number: two Kalanj households sharing house 188, the same shape this file keeps meeting with Borić households at Kamenica 23 and 24. The surname here reads Kalanj clearly in this hand, and the mother's Krnarić is one of the surnames Borić women also marry into. Not merged with the Viol Kalanj household.
Stipe Kalanj, son of Mijo Kalanj and Krnarić Manda||son of Kalanj Mijo and Krnarić Manda, of Brinje house 249 - the first child on record of that marriage - not in the tree|baptism|18 November 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 483, entry no. 137 - "KALANJ STIPE", male, born 18 and registered 20 November 1899, of Brinje house 249, son of KALANJ MIJO and KRNARIĆ MANDA. Witnesses Vučetić Stipe i KALANJ LUCE, matičar Vučetić Stipe. Later marginal notes of 1982-83 record the child's own later civil events (not fully read). NOT IN THE TREE. THE CHILD OF A MARRIAGE ALREADY IN THIS FILE: Mijo Kalanj, bachelor, 55, of Brinje house 249, married Krnarić Manda (Manoš), spinster, 23, daughter of Krnarić Jure of house 168, in 1893 (marriage book, image 566, this file) - the same two parents' names, the same house, six years on. Mijo would be about 61 at this birth; the file's earlier note gives him as born about 1838, so he is an old father but not an impossible one. TWO THINGS FOLLOW. First, the house number 249 is also where this archive logged a Kalauj Jure and Vučetić Ove/Manole in 1892 (image 171) as a distinct near-miss family: a house that holds a Kalanj bachelor of 55 in 1893 and a Kalanj baby in 1899 also holds a 'Kalauj' household in between, which is a point in favour of reading that household as Kalanj, and is recorded here as such a point and not as a reclassification. Second, the witness KALANJ LUCE is a Kalanj woman not otherwise known to this file, probably a kinswoman of Mijo. NOT merged with any other Kalanj household.
Luce Kalanj, witness at Brinje house 249||witness to the baptism of Kalanj Stipe, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|20 November 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 483, entry no. 137 - the baptism of "KALANJ STIPE", male, of Brinje house 249, son of Kalanj Mijo and Krnarić Manda, names "KALANJ LUCE" as a witness alongside Vučetić Stipe. NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only - a first Kalanj woman named Luce in this file (read as Kalanj; the Kalanj/Kalauj doubt is settled, they are the same); at the house of Mijo Kalanj, so most likely a relative of the child's father standing up for him.
Marija Kalanj, witness at Brinje house 228||witness to the baptism of Murat Jure, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|20 December 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries numbering within calendar year 1899), image 485, entry no. 148 - the baptism of "MURAT JURE", male, born 17 and registered 20 December 1899, of Brinje house 228, son of Murat Jure and Rajković Marija, names "KALANJ MARIJA" as a witness alongside a Petrović Ove (surname read with some doubt). NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only, the Kalanj/Kalauj doubt once carried here is settled (Kalauj is Kalanj, 5 October 2026). The given name Marija is that of Marija Vučetić, wife of Niko Kalanj of house 231 (this file), and of the Marija of the 1899 Vučetić-mother Kalanj entries at that house; whether this is that woman standing witness at another household is a plausible, unconfirmed link, not a merge.
Manole Borić, daughter of Grgo Borić and Marija Milaković (house 126)||daughter of Grgo Borić and Milaković Marija, of Brinje house 126 - a third child of that household - not in the tree|baptism|30 December 1899|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih (third item on the same film as DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S, entries running to the end of the 1899 sequence and booked on 1 January), image 487, entry no. 155 - "BORIĆ MANOLE", female, born 30 December 1899 and registered 1 January (year written as 1899 in the entry, most likely 1900 by the date), of Brinje house 126, daughter of BORIĆ GRGO and MILAKOVIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses Blažanin Viol i Manola, matičar Vučetić Stipe. NOT IN THE TREE. A THIRD CHILD of the Grgo Borić and Marija Milaković household already in this file (Stjepan, born August 1893; Ana, born 25 December 1894), at the same house number, 126, and with both parents' names exactly as before - five years after the last child. This is the steadiest Grgo Borić household in the file, and the one that carries the Borić Grgo witness at house 74 (this file) only by the shared given name; whether those men are the same is still not established. The father is entered as Grgo, not Ivan or Ive, so the Ivan/Ive Borić of house 126 (father of Juko and the widow Luce, this file) is again not this man's household. Kept apart from the other Manole Borić in this file (daughter of Alojz Borić, house 23).
Pave Kalanj, son of Viol Kalanj and Kate Zoričić||son of Viol Kalanj and Zoričić Kate, of Brinje house 188 - the second child of that household, missed on the first pass - not in the tree|baptism|14 January 1892|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 163, entry no. 9 - "KALANJ PAVE", male, born 14 January and registered 17 January 1892, of Brinje house 188, son of KALANJ VIOL and ZORIČIĆ KATE. Witnesses Perkić Mijo (the recurring near-miss) i Dražanović Manda, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND ON 5 OCTOBER 2026 WHILE SETTLING THE KALAUJ QUESTION: this entry was read at the time as a Kalauj near-miss and so never recorded. It is a clear Kalanj in a clean hand, and it is the missing middle child of the Viol Kalanj x Zoričić Kate household already in this file - Kate (December 1890, house 118), PAVE (January 1892, house 188), Franjo (August 1893, house 189) and Marija (March 1899, house 188) - and it shows the house number 188 belongs to this household from 1892, which explains the 188 of the 1899 entries and settles the 118/189/188 drift noted earlier as a scribe's habit with one house. The Kalanj household of Jerko Kalanj and Krnarić Ruže at house 188 in 1899 (this file) therefore shares a house with the Viol household for at least seven years.
Marija Kalanj, daughter of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Manole (house 231, 1891)||daughter of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Manole, of Brinje house 231 - the household earlier filed as 'Kalauj' - not in the tree|baptism|22 November 1891|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 157, entry no. 158 - "KALANJ MARISA" (given name read as Marisa, probably a diminutive of Marija), female, born 22 and registered 26 November 1891, of Brinje house 231, daughter of KALANJ JURE and VUČETIĆ MANOLE. Witnesses Čalac(?) Joso i Rumenović Kate, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. THIS ENTRY SETTLES THE KALAUJ QUESTION. It was read in September 2026 as 'Kalauj' and logged as a distinct near-miss family. Re-read at full zoom on 5 October 2026 the surname is KALANJ in every letter - the same word as the unmistakable Kalanj Viol at image 163 - and the parents (Jure, mother Vučetić Manole), the house (231, Niko Kalanj's own house) and the entry's formulae are exactly those of the 1899 birth of Ruže Kalanj (image 450). The 'Kalauj' family does not exist as a separate family: it is the Jure Kalanj x Vučetić Manole household of house 231, with Niko Kalanj (married 1890 to a widow Marija, later entered Vučetić) and a Kalanj Mile x Vučetić Marija at the same house, all inside one Kalanj family.
Marko Kalanj, son of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Ove (1892)||son of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Ove, of Brinje house 249 - second child of the household earlier filed as 'Kalauj' - not in the tree|baptism|14 May 1892|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 171, entry no. 42 - "KALANJ MARKO", male, born 14 and registered 15 May 1892, of Brinje house 249, son of KALANJ JURE and VUČETIĆ OVE (Ove/Ave, a short form of Manole as the same woman's name shifts between her children's entries). Witness Trölich Jure i Marija, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. Read in September 2026 as a 'Kalauj' entry and kept out of this file; re-read at full zoom on 5 October 2026 the word is plainly KALANJ, in the same hand as the header of entry 42 itself ('Kalanj Marko'). Second child of the Jure Kalanj x Vučetić household (Marija/Marisa 1891 at house 231, this file; Ruže 1899 at house 231, this file), now at house 249, where Mijo Kalanj (this file) lived. Kalanj men at 249 and 231 are thus one family's two houses.
Petar Kalanj, son of Tome Kalanj and Nesić Marija||son of Tome Kalanj and Nesić (read with some doubt) Marija, of Brinje house 188 - a third Kalanj household at that house number - not in the tree|baptism|14 November 1891|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 155, entry no. 150 - "KALANJ PETAR", male, born 14 and registered 15 November 1891, of Brinje house 188, son of KALANJ TOME and NESIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses Perlić Mijo (the near-miss) i Dražanović Marija, matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. A THIRD KALANJ FATHER at house 188 after Viol (Kate 1890, Pave 1892, Marija 1899, this file) and Jerko (Manole 1899, this file): Tome. House 188 is now a Kalanj house with three heads in eight years. Not merged with either.
Ove Kalanj, daughter of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Manole (house 231, 1894)||daughter of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Manole, of Brinje house 231 - the third child of the household earlier filed as 'Kalauj' - not in the tree|baptism|14 February 1894|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 259, entry no. 76 - "KALANJ OVE", female, born 14 and registered 16 February 1894, of Brinje house 231, daughter of KALANJ JURE and VUČETIĆ MANOLE. Witnesses Dražanović Marko i Luce, a later marginal note of 1978. NOT IN THE TREE. Read in September 2026 as a 'Kalauj' entry and kept out of this file; at full zoom on 5 October 2026 the surname is KALANJ and the parents and house are those of Marija/Marisa (1891) and of Ruže (1899), this file. The Jure Kalanj x Vučetić Manole household at house 231 is thus now four children over eight years: Marija/Marisa 1891, Marko 1892 (house 249), Ove 1894 and Ruže 1899.
Mile Kalanj and Marija, witnesses at Lučane (1894)||witnesses to the baptism of Marinović Manda, of Lučane - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|December 1894|Lučane, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 274 (the shown frame is the one after 273; entry 143, Lučane, Marinović Manda, daughter of Marinović Ivan and Šakić(?) Marija; dates read at reduced zoom as born about 2 and registered about 6 December 1894), witness line read "KALANJ MILE i Marija" (the surname read with the usual doubt in this hand, here the mother of the child is not Kalanj). NOT IN THE TREE. A witness pair only. The given names are those of the couple who appear in 1899 as parents of Franc Kalanj at house 231 (Kalanj Mile x Vučetić Marija, this file): if the same pair, they were witnessing at a Lučane baptism five years before their own child's, which is a plausible, unconfirmed link and not a merge. Another sign that the people this register once read as 'Kalauj' are Kalanj kin.
Manole Kalanj, daughter of Mijo Kalanj and Krnarić Manole (1895)||daughter of Mijo Kalanj and Krnarić Manole, of Brinje house 249 - a child of the 1893 marriage, missed on the first pass - not in the tree|baptism|10 January 1895|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 281 (the shown frame follows 280), entry no. 11 - "KALANJ MANOLE", female, born 10 and registered 13 January 1895, of Brinje house 249, daughter of KALANJ MIJO and KRNARIĆ MANOLE. Witnesses Trölich Jure i Marija, matičar Sertić Šimun; a later marginal note of 1949. NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND ON 5 OCTOBER 2026 WHILE SETTLING THE KALAUJ QUESTION, in the same stretch the earlier pass had logged as Kalauj near-misses. It is a clear Kalanj in the clean hand of this entry. A child of the marriage of Mijo Kalanj and Krnarić Manda (1893, this file), between the 1893 wedding and Stipe (1899, this file): Mijo's household at house 249 is now two children deep, and the SAME WITNESSES, Trölich Jure i Marija, stood at the 1892 birth of Kalanj Marko at the same house (this file) - one neighbourhood and one set of witnesses for both the Jure Kalanj and the Mijo Kalanj households at house 249.
Kate Borić, wife of Petar Sertić (1895)||mother of Sertić Stjepan, of Brinje house 128 - an earlier child of the Petar Sertić x Kate Borić household - not in the tree|birth of a child|11 November 1895|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 313 (the shown frame follows 312), entry no. 136 - "SERTIĆ STJEPAN", male, born 11 and registered 13 November 1895, of Brinje house 128, son of SERTIĆ PETAR and BORIĆ KATE. Witnesses Lasić Stjepan i BORIĆ JELA, matičar Sertić. NOT IN THE TREE. MISSED ON THE FIRST PASS and found on 5 October 2026 while re-reading the 300-318 stretch that the earlier log had recorded as 'no new finds' - a Borić mother and a Borić witness in a single entry that the fit-zoom reading did not catch. It is the FIRST child on record of the household whose 1899 child Tomo is in this file (Kate Borić, wife of Petar Sertić, Brinje house 128, born 7 August 1899): the same father, mother and house number, four years earlier, which turns that 1899 row from a single sighting into a household.
Jela Borić, witness at Brinje house 128 (1895)||witness to the baptism of Sertić Stjepan, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|13 November 1895|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 313, entry no. 136 - the baptism of "SERTIĆ STJEPAN", male, of Brinje house 128, son of Sertić Petar and Borić Kate, names "BORIĆ JELA" as a witness alongside Lasić Stjepan. NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only, and the same Borić woman who stood witness at the next baptism in the Sertić-Borić line, at house 128 on 13 August 1899 (this file): a Jela Borić recurring at the Sertić Petar household four years apart is the plainest sign that she is Kate's kinswoman, perhaps her sister or mother, but the entries do not say so and she is not merged with the Jela Borić of Tome Borić's household at house 141.
Luce Borić, wife of Tome Karakaš (1895)||mother of Karakaš Joso, of Brinje house 220 - a Borić woman married to a Karakaš, not in the tree|birth of a child|7 November 1895|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 317 (page 236 of the register; the viewer shows the frame after 316), entry no. 152 - "KARAKAŠ JOSO", male, born 7 and registered 10 November 1895, of Brinje house 220, son of KARAKAŠ TOME and BORIĆ LUCE, both of Brinje, farmers, Croats. Informants read "Borić Ivica i Jela", matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND ON 5 OCTOBER 2026 on the readable-zoom re-read of the 300-318 stretch, which the first pass had logged as 'no new finds'. Read at high zoom: the mother's surname is the same Borić form as the Borić entries elsewhere in this register, not Đorić. A Borić woman whose child carries her husband's Karakaš name, so a search on Borić as a child's surname would never find it; it surfaces only as a mother or a witness. She is not placed in any Borić household here, and she is not merged with the Luce Borić of Tome Borić's house 141 (a daughter baptised 1899) or the Luce Borić wife of Pave Sertić.
Ivica Borić and Jela, informants at Brinje house 220 (1895)||named as informants (prijavitelji) at the birth of Karakaš Joso, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|10 November 1895|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 317, entry no. 152 - the line for the informants reads "Borić Ivica i Jela" at the birth of KARAKAŠ JOSO, son of Karakaš Tome and Borić Luce, Brinje house 220. NOT IN THE TREE. Two Borić names in the place of the child's maternal kin, most plausibly the mother's parents or a brother and his wife, but the entry does not say so. The surname was checked at high zoom (Borić, not Đorić). The given name Jela recurs among the Boriće of this register (Tome Borić's wife at house 141; a witness at house 128 in 1895 and 1899) and is NOT merged with any of them.
Manda Borić, wife of Ivo Petrinić (1895)||mother of Petrinić Marija, of Brinje house 16 - a Borić woman married to a Petrinić, not in the tree|birth of a child|20 October 1895|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 314 (page 230 of the register; the viewer shows the frame after 313), entry no. 140 - "PETRINIĆ MARIJA", female, born and registered 20 October 1895, of Brinje house 16, daughter of PETRINIĆ IVO and BORIĆ MANDA, both of Brinje, farmers, Croats. Witnesses read "Jakov Luka i Marija", matičar Sertić. A later marginal note records a marriage contracted on 14 September 1914 and a registry entry of 1973. NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND ON 5 OCTOBER 2026 on the readable-zoom re-read of the 300-318 stretch; the first pass had read this spread at fit zoom and logged it as 'no new finds'. The mother's surname was read at high zoom and is Borić, a Borić woman married out under her husband's Petrinić name, so a search on Borić as a child's surname never finds it. She is not placed in any Borić household and is not merged with any Manda or Manole Borić in this file.
Perković wife of Marko Vuković, mother of Vuković Joso (1895)||mother of Vuković Joso, of Brinje - the Perković bride of the 1893 Vuković marriage, now with a child on record - not in the tree|birth of a child|9 November 1895|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 317 (page 236; the viewer shows the frame after 316), entry no. 153 - "VUKOVIĆ JOSO", male, born 9 and registered 10 November 1895, of Brinje (house number read as 103, probably 105 - not clear), son of VUKOVIĆ MARKO and a mother whose surname is written in the hand's 'Perkonić' form (given name read 'Bare' or 'Dare', probably the same name that the marriage entry abbreviates as Đuso), both of Brinje, farmers, Croats. Informants "Kalafatić Mijo i Manda", matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND ON 5 OCTOBER 2026 ON THE RE-READ OF THE 300-318 STRETCH, WHERE THE FIRST PASS HAD FILED THE MOTHER'S SURNAME AS THE 'PERHONIĆ' NEAR-MISS. THAT FILING WAS WRONG HERE. The entry is the child of the marriage already in this file (image 581, Vuković Marko x Perković Đuso, 1893, bride of Brinje house 145, father Perković Jozo): the same father, a mother of the same surname, and the SAME WITNESS, Kalafatić Mijo, who stood at the wedding and is the informant here. And the hand writes its v like an n throughout - the father's own name on the same page is written 'Vukonić' for Vuković - so 'Perkonić' is Perković. The recurring 'Perhonić' of the earlier log is therefore OPEN, not settled: it is at least in part the Perković surname, and every earlier Perhonić sighting has to be re-read before the family page can say how many Perković households Brinje holds.
Luce Kalanj, daughter of Jure Kalanj (house 231, 1889)||daughter of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Manole, of Brinje house 231 - the eldest child of that household found so far, born before the 1891 Marija - not in the tree|baptism|28 December 1889|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 84 (the viewer shows the frame after 83), entry no. 155, the LAST entry of 1889 - "KALANJ LUCE", female, born 25 and registered 28 December 1889, of Brinje house 231, daughter of KALANJ JURE and VUČETIĆ MANOLE, both of Brinje, farmers, Croats. Informants "Rumenović Tomo i Stoja", matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND ON 5 OCTOBER 2026 ON THE READABLE-ZOOM RE-READ, IN A STRETCH (images 1-299) THE FIRST PASS HAD LOGGED AS READ. A clear Kalanj in a clean hand, missed at spread-fit zoom. It is the same house 231, father Jure and mother Vučetić Manole as the 1891 Marija, the 1892 Marko, the 1894 Ove and the 1899 Ruže Kalanj (this file), so that household now has five children on record across ten years, 1889-1899, and Luce is the oldest. The informant Rumenović Tomo is the same Rimenović Tomo who witnessed the 1890 marriage of Niko Kalanj of house 231 (this file). It is also the name 'Luce Kalanj' that recurs as a witness at house 249 in 1899 (this file), which is a named link, not a proven one: she would have been nine.
Nikola Perković, son of Mile Perković and Marica Perković (Križpolje 22, 1893)||son of Mile Perković and Marica, both of the Perković surname, of Križpolje house 22 - a Perković household in a hamlet of the Brinje parish, not in the tree|baptism|21 October 1893|Križpolje, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1888-1900 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 233 (the viewer shows the frame after 232), entry no. 138 - the birth of a boy, born 19 and registered 21 October 1893, whose own name and both parents' surnames are written in the hand's 'Perkonić' form: "PERKOVIĆ NIKOLA", son of PERKOVIĆ MILE and PERKOVIĆ MARICA, both of Križpolje house 22, farmers, Croats. Informants "Hranović Niko i Antija", matičar Rubelli Lavoslav (the matičar of 1893; Sertić Šimun signs from 1895). NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND AS A MIS-FILING ON 5 OCTOBER 2026: the first pass logged this entry on 29 September as a possible Perković that 'turned out to be Perhonić, a distinct surname already met twice before'. It was not distinct. The hand writes v like n (the Vuković of the 1893 Vuković-Perković marriage reads 'Vukonić' on the same page as its Perković bride, image 581, and the father at image 317 entry 153 is the same Vuković Marko), so 'Perkonić' is Perković, and this is a Perković household: a father Mile and a mother Marica who both carry the surname, so either two Perković kin who married or a mother recorded under her husband's name - the entry does not say which. It is a different household from Marko, Pere and Miko Perković of Novi Kut and from Jozo Perković of house 145 (this file), and its house number is at Križpolje, not Brinje town.
Jure Kalanj, son of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Ane (1896)||son of Jure Kalanj and Vučetić Ane, of Brinje house 249 - a Kalanj child of 1896 with a Vučetić mother, in the stretch the first pass marked as Kalauj near-misses - not in the tree|baptism|20 September 1896|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 351 (entered as 351 in the viewer, whose own frame label reads one lower), entry no. 111 (the figure is partly cut in the frame) - "KALANJ JURE", male, born 14 and registered 20 September 1896, of Brinje house 249, son of KALANJ JURE and VUČETIĆ ANE (the mother's given name is the one this file also reads as Manole, Ove or Ane in her other children's entries), both of Brinje, farmers, Croats. Informants "Vučetić Joso i Manda", matičar Tausani Josip. NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND ON 5 OCTOBER 2026 ON THE RE-READ OF IMAGES 351-355. A clear Kalanj in a clean hand, and the first of the five-image range the earlier log named for Kalauj sightings that was actually re-read. The couple is the Jure Kalanj and Vučetić woman of the Brinje house-231 household already in this file (Luce 1889, Marija 1891, Marko 1892, Ove 1894, Ruže 1899), a gap between the 1894 and 1899 children: the 1896 entry gives the house as 249 (the number of Mijo Kalanj's household), where the other five children give 231 - either the house number drifted or the family moved, and the entry does not say which, so this is recorded as the same couple on name and mother's surname, not merged as one proven household. The informant Vučetić Joso is the mother's own surname, plausibly her brother or father.
Kate Borić, daughter of Tome Borić and Jela Borić (house 141, 1896)||daughter of Tome Borić and Jela Borić, of Brinje house 141 - a sixth child of that household, whose own register note gives her married name as Perković - not in the tree|baptism|7 October 1896|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 354 (entered as 354 in the viewer; page 310 of the register), entry no. 122 (read as 122; the entry below it is plainly 123) - "BORIĆ KATE", female, born 6 and registered 7 October 1896, of Brinje house 141, daughter of BORIĆ TOME and BORIĆ JELA, both of Brinje, farmers, Croats. Informants "Perkić Mijo i Borić Marija", matičar Sertić Šimun. A later marginal note in a different hand reads, at full zoom, "umrla 2/IV 1917 g." (died 2 April 1917) followed by "Perković rođ." (née) - the surname before 'rođ.' is read as Perković with moderate confidence, the 1917 hand being a different one. NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND ON 5 OCTOBER 2026 ON THE RE-READ OF IMAGES 351-355. It is the sixth child on record of the Tome Borić x Jela Borić household of house 141 (Juraj 1888, Petar 1890, Matija 1892, Ove 1894, Luce 1899, this file), between Ove and Luce. Two facts make it matter beyond the count: (1) the 1917 note, if read right, says she married a Perković and died at twenty, a documented Borić-Perković marriage in this parish, which no other row in this file yet holds; (2) the informant is the Perkić Mijo who recurs as a witness at Borić births across the volume (the Stjepan Borić baptism of 1890, the Krnarić and Mesić baptisms of 1899, this file), so that man is now tied to the Borić households as well as to the surname the first pass kept apart from Perković. She is not merged with the Kate Borić who is a wife in the Sertić household of house 128, nor with any other Kate.
Marija Kalanj, wife of Ivan Mesić (1896)||mother of Mesić Manole, of Brinje house 176 - a Kalanj woman married into the Mesić surname, not in the tree|birth of a child|21 October 1896|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 355 (entered as 355 in the viewer; page 313), entry no. 128 - "MESIĆ MANOLE", female, born 20 and registered 21 October 1896, of Brinje house 176, daughter of MESIĆ IVAN and KALANJ MARIJA, both of Brinje, farmers, Croats. Informants "Rumenović Tomo i Kalanj Manda", matičar Sertić Šimun. NOT IN THE TREE. FOUND ON 5 OCTOBER 2026 ON THE RE-READ OF IMAGES 351-355, in the range where the earlier log placed Kalauj sightings. The mother's surname is a clear Kalanj in a clean hand, the same 'Kalanj' as the surrounding Kalanj entries on this register. A third Kalanj woman who married out of the surname (after the Ane Kalanj of Dražičević and the Ane Kalanj of Krmarić, this file). The informant Rumenović Tomo is the same man who stood at the 1889 birth of Luce Kalanj (house 231) and at the 1890 marriage of Niko Kalanj of house 231 (this file), so this Mesić-Kalanj household sits inside the same circle of Kalanj families. Her father is not named by the entry and she is not linked to any Kalanj household here.
Manda Kalanj, informant at Brinje house 176 (1896)||named as an informant at the birth of Mesić Manole, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|21 October 1896|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 355, entry no. 128 - the informants' line reads "Rumenović Tomo i Kalanj Manda" at the birth of Mesić Manole, whose mother is Kalanj Marija. NOT IN THE TREE. A Kalanj woman named as an informant beside Rumenović Tomo, plausibly the mother's kinswoman, perhaps her sister or mother, but the entry does not say; the given name is read Manda, which this file also meets as Manole (Mijo Kalanj's wife Krnarić Manda and the Vučetić Manole of house 231), and she is not merged with either of them.
